WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们会剖析《办公室》的一集，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能讲述的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

8
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.130
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.350
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

10
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.550
I am very excited because I absolutely love this episode.
我非常兴奋，因为我太喜欢这一集了。

11
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.930
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

12
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.130
I'm so excited to talk about it.
我迫不及待地想聊聊它。

13
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.170
This had remnants of the duel for me.
这让我想起了《决斗》那一集的感觉。

14
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.550
I remember loving the duel.
我记得我很喜欢《决斗》那一集。

15
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:38.930
It's great.
真的很棒。

16
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.450
I can't wait, too.
我也迫不及待了。

17
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.790
You know how much I loved all these scenes with Oscar.
你知道我有多喜欢所有这些有奥斯卡的场景。

18
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:43.750
Let's get to it.
我们开始吧。

19
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:52.490
We are talking about The Target, Season 9, Episode 8, written by Graham Wagner and directed by Brent Forrester.
我们要聊的是《目标》，第九季第八集，由格雷厄姆·瓦格纳编剧，布伦特·福雷斯特执导。

20
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.150
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

21
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.350
Oscar isn't sure if Angela knows about his affair with the senator.
奥斯卡不确定安吉拉是否知道他和参议员有染。

22
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.350
But in reality, oh, boy, does she know.
但现实中，天呐，她怎么可能不知道。

23
00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:05.610
And she has enlisted Dwight's help to exact her revenge.
而且她已经请来德怀特帮忙实施报复。

24
00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:12.550
Jim is going to go to great lengths to be granted permission to work part-time in Scranton.
吉姆将不遗余力地争取获得在斯克兰顿兼职工作的许可。

25
00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:18.330
And Pete's meaningless office task ends up being a fun project that unites his coworkers.
皮特无足轻重的办公室任务最终成了一个有趣的活动，将同事们团结在了一起。

26
00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.450
Can I just say that Pete is the new Jim?
我能说皮特就是新吉姆吗？

27
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.470
I literally wrote down in the breakdown that I am in love with Pete.
我在大纲里甚至直接写了，我爱上皮特了。

28
00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.690
But just how he got everyone to do this activity, it's Office Olympics.
但就凭他是怎么让所有人都参与这个活动的，这简直就是办公室奥运会。

29
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:33.250
Yes.
没错。

30
00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:34.710
It's Jim and Office Olympics.
这就是吉姆和办公室奥运会。

31
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:35.150
Yes.
对。

32
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:35.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

33
00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:36.530
All right.
好吧。

34
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.970
Fast fact number one.
趣事一号。

35
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.290
Chris Gethard is our special guest star playing Trevor.
克里斯·格哈德是我们的特别客串明星，饰演特雷弗。

36
00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.350
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

37
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.870
I have so many stories.
我有超多故事要讲。

38
00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.310
We got so much mail.
我们收到了海量的邮件。

39
00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.410
Fan question from Lindsay H.
来自亚利桑那州坦佩市的林赛·H的粉丝提问，她说：

40
00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.650
in Tempe, Arizona, who said,
来自亚利桑那州坦佩市的林赛·H说，

41
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.990
I just wanted to show appreciation for the genius that is the character Trevor,
我只是想对特雷弗这个角色的天才之处表示赞赏，

42
00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.530
played by the awesome comedian Chris Gethard.
这个角色由出色的喜剧演员克里斯·格哈德饰演。

43
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:03.150
He did such a great job embodying the sort of dazed weirdo that was Trevor
他把特雷弗那种茫然的怪咖形象演绎得淋漓尽致，

44
00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.190
and was so funny in spite of only appearing in two episodes.
而且尽管只出场了两集，却依然非常搞笑。

45
00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.730
And then Wendy B.
然后是来自马里兰州贝塞斯达的温迪·B说，

46
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.890
from Bethesda, Maryland, said,
然后是温迪·B，

47
00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.110
I got such a kick out of Chris Gethard as Trevor.
克里斯·格哈德饰演的特雷弗让我觉得太逗了。

48
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.350
He was strange and hilarious.
他又古怪又滑稽。

49
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.390
How did he wind up being cast?
他是怎么被选中出演的呢？

50
00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.330
Well, Lindsay and Wendy, thanks for writing in.
嗯，林赛和温迪，谢谢你们来信。

51
00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.590
Yes, Chris is so amazing and very unique.
没错，克里斯太棒了，而且非常有特色。

52
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.150
And Angela, you got to work with him.
安吉拉，你还和他合作过。

53
00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:27.630
Yes.
是的。

54
00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.070
You said it was so fun.
你说过这太有趣了。

55
00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:34.170
And you also reached out to him, and he sent us in some audio clips.
而且你还主动联系了他，他给我们发来了一些音频片段。

56
00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:34.790
I did.
我是联系了。

57
00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.110
He was so great.
他真的太棒了。

58
00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.190
You know when you write someone and they respond back right away and are like,
你知道当你给某人发消息，他们立刻回复并说

59
00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.270
yes, I'm in.
好的，我加入。

60
00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:41.750
Yes.
是的。

61
00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:42.290
That was Chris.
那就是克里斯。

62
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.170
Well, of course, the first thing we asked was,
当然，我们问的第一个问题是

63
00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.710
how did you get your role on The Office?
你是怎么得到《办公室》里的角色的？

64
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.170
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的讲述。

65
00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:49.510
Hi, everybody.
大家好。

66
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.370
My name's Chris Gethard.
我叫克里斯·格瑟德。

67
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:56.530
And I was really lucky to play a character named Trevor on The Office just for a couple episodes.
我很幸运能在《办公室》里客串几集，饰演一个叫特雷弗的角色。

68
00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.170
But sometimes I think people think I was on it more than I was
但有时我觉得大家认为我出现的集数比实际更多

69
00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.130
based on the amount that they talked to me about it.
就凭他们跟我聊起这事的频率来看。

70
00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.470
But it was a really lucky experience.
但这真的是一次幸运的经历。

71
00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.950
And I think about it a lot.
我经常想起它。

72
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.650
And I feel so lucky to be here talking about it today.
今天能在这里谈论它，我感到非常幸运。

73
00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.450
How did I get my role on The Office?
我是怎么得到《办公室》里的角色的？

74
00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.230
I've never totally been sure.
我其实一直不太确定。

75
00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.130
I auditioned.
我试镜了。

76
00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.190
I know that much.
这一点我很确定。

77
00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.730
I've always been East Coast based.
我的大本营一直在东海岸。

78
00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.890
I grew up in New Jersey and came up at the Upright Citizens Brigade in New York.
我在新泽西长大，在纽约的正气公民剧团（UCB）崭露头角。

79
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:33.570
I remember that I filmed my audition for The Office at the Manhattan Neighborhood Network,
我记得我是在曼哈顿社区网络录制《办公室》试镜视频的，

80
00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:37.570
which is the public access studio in New York City.
那是纽约市的一个公共频道制片室。

81
00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.450
And it's kind of legendarily weird, all the stuff that comes out of there.
从那里出来的内容各种各样，可以说是传奇般的古怪。

82
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.370
And I did a talk show there for many years.
我在那里做过很多年脱口秀。

83
00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:47.510
I know I was on Alison Jones' radar to some degree.
我知道自己某种程度上进入了选角导演艾莉森·琼斯的视线。

84
00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.530
I was actually in an improv group in New York with Bobby Moynihan and Zach Woods.
我其实和鲍比·莫伊尼汉以及扎克·伍兹在纽约组过一个即兴喜剧团。

85
00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.690
Zach Woods obviously played Gabe on The Office.
扎克·伍兹显然在《办公室》里饰演了盖比。

86
00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.330
And you can imagine being with those guys at UCB at the time.
你可以想象当时和这群人在UCB共事的情景。

87
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.750
There was just a lot of eyes on us.
当时有很多人在关注我们。

88
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.990
So mostly I just auditioned and got lucky.
所以基本上我就是去试镜，然后运气好被选上了。

89
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:06.610
And I've always kind of wondered who championed me over there,
我其实一直很好奇那边是谁在力挺我，

90
00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.290
if it was Alison or one of the writers,
是艾莉森还是某位编剧，

91
00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.110
just because I knew a lot of people from my time in comedy.
只是因为我在喜剧界混的这段时间认识了很多人。

92
00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:15.830
This answer is very rambly, but I mean, you ask an actor how they got a role.
这个回答非常天马行空，不过说真的，你问一个演员他是怎么得到一个角色的。

93
00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.730
The answer always sort of comes down to, I don't know,
答案往往归结为，我不知道，

94
00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:25.090
but it's some combination of UCB and having some hype from my public access show,
但这是UCB的经历、我的公共频道脱口秀带来的一些热度，

95
00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.910
having done a couple other things at that point in time,
以及当时已经做过的一些其他事情的综合结果，

96
00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:34.270
but mostly just auditioned and sent in a tape and then felt really lucky that they went with me.
但主要还是去试镜并交了录像带，然后为他们最终选了我感到非常幸运。

97
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.290
Chris, we love a rambly.
克里斯，我们可太喜欢天马行空的回答了。

98
00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.250
Ramble as much as you want.
你想怎么天马行空地聊都行。

99
00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:43.250
You know what I love about that story is that we were still,
你知道我最喜欢那个故事的哪一点吗，就是我们当时还在

100
00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.470
oh, Sam, you are so kind.
噢，萨姆，你太好了。

101
00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.530
Did he bring you a tissue so you don't have to leave?
他给你拿纸巾去了，好让你不用离开吗？

102
00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.110
He's bringing me tissue.
他正在给我拿纸巾呢。

103
00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:48.930
Use your sleeve.
用你的袖子擦呗。

104
00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.270
I was using my sleeve to wipe my nose.
我刚才就是用袖子擦鼻涕来着。

105
00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.090
And I don't, all of a sudden it started running.
然后我就不知道，它突然就开始流了。

106
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:53.770
I don't know.
我也不知道。

107
00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.090
It's the weather.
都是这天气闹的。

108
00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.090
It is.
确实。

109
00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:59.930
It's the weird cold, the cold LA.
这是一种奇怪的冷，洛杉矶式的寒冷。

110
00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.330
It's very, what would you call it?
这非常……你管这叫什么？

111
00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.930
We had frost this morning.
我们今天早上还结霜了呢。

112
00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:10.790
Yeah, it's a weird cold snap that happens in the LA winter and it happens suddenly and then my nose just runs.
对啊，洛杉矶的冬天就是有这种奇怪的寒流，说来就来，然后我的鼻子就开始流涕。

113
00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.730
Okay, thank you, everyone.
好啦，谢谢大家。

114
00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:21.910
What I was going to say was, I love the part of that story that makes it so obvious that we were still going to New York to find actors.
我想说的是，那个故事里最妙的一点在于，它清楚地表明我们当时依然要去纽约寻找演员。

115
00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:27.110
Like, at this point, nine years in, I feel like Alison Jones could have just been phoning it in.
就好比，到了这个时候，已经合作第九年了，我觉得艾莉森·琼斯本可以随便敷衍了事的。

116
00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:27.830
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

117
00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.130
Not Alison Jones.
但那可是艾莉森·琼斯。

118
00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:29.610
No.
没错。

119
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.090
No.
不是的。

120
00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:35.230
She's like, I still want to know who are the hottest people in comedy and improv.
她心想：我还是想知道喜剧和即兴表演界现在最火的是谁。

121
00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.750
I don't care what city they're living in.
我才不管他们住在哪个城市。

122
00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:37.750
I need to see them.
我必须见到他们。

123
00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:38.070
Yeah.
是啊。

124
00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:39.970
That's it right there.
就是这样。

125
00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.390
I think mystery solved.
我想谜题解开了。

126
00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.590
It's Alison Jones.
这就是艾莉森·琼斯。

127
00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:43.650
It's Alison Jones.
这就是艾莉森·琼斯。

128
00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.750
Just doing her job so well.
只是把工作做得太出色了。

129
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.390
And then Chris showing up.
然后克里斯就出现了。

130
00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.570
Oh, well, of course.
噢，那当然。

131
00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:55.910
But, you know, half of getting parts as an actor is the access, the opportunity.
不过呢，演员能得到角色，有一半靠的是人脉和机会。

132
00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:56.830
Getting your foot in the door.
也就是敲开那扇门。

133
00:05:57.010 --> 00:06:03.670
Yeah, you have to be ready, but it's my old acting teacher used to say, success is opportunity meets readiness.
对，你必须时刻准备着，但就像我以前的表演老师常说的，成功就是机会与准备的结合。

134
00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:08.530
You can get all the auditions in the world, but if you're not ready for them, you're not going to go anywhere.
你可以得到世上所有的试镜机会，但如果你没有准备好，也是走不远的。

135
00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:15.770
Similarly, you can be the greatest actor in your living room, but if you have no opportunities, again, opportunity meets readiness.
同理，你在自己家里可以是个最伟大的演员，但如果你没有任何机会——还是那句话，机会遇上准备。

136
00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.710
I think that's good for just life.
我觉得这对生活也很有道理。

137
00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.150
Because imagine if you're going in for a job interview, it's the same thing.
因为想象一下，如果你去参加工作面试，也是一回事。

138
00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:26.270
You can have all the skill set, but if you can't get in the room, I want to be in the room where it happens.
你可以具备所有的技能，但如果你进不了那个房间——我想进到那个发生一切的房间里。

139
00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:27.370
The room where it happens.
那个发生一切的房间。

140
00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.210
We go back to Hamilton.
我们又扯回《汉密尔顿》了。

141
00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.190
Always.
每次都这样。

142
00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:30.650
Always.
每次都是。

143
00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:36.190
You know, Angela, you said that when you emailed Chris, he responded right away, and he was so nice and so receptive.
安吉拉，你知道的，你刚才说过当你给克里斯发邮件时，他立刻就回复了，而且他人特别好，非常乐意配合。

144
00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:46.990
I have to share with people that Chris told us that the reason he was so happy to send an audio clips was because you were so nice to him on set, and he never forgot it.
我必须跟大家好好分享一下，克里斯告诉我们，他之所以这么乐意发送音频片段，是因为你在片场对人太好了，他一直没忘。

145
00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:53.850
He actually shared that you were so nice that he was kind of confused at first because he only knew you as Angela Martin.
他还分享说，你人实在是太好了，以至于他一开始甚至有点糊涂，因为他只知道你是安吉拉·马丁。

146
00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.910
Here is how he described it.
他是这样描述的。

147
00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:03.050
I was on season nine, and like everybody else in America, I had watched the first eight.
当时我在拍第九季，和美国的所有人一样，前八季我全都看过。

148
00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.090
So you do forget, like, people are humans.
所以你有时会忘记，原来大家都是活生生的人。

149
00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.210
They're well-rounded humans.
他们是性格全面的人。

150
00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:14.410
So I will say anytime Angela would ever ask me to do anything, I would, of course, say yes because she was so kind on set.
所以我要说的是，不管什么时候只要安吉拉叫我做什么，我当然都会答应，因为她在片场太善良了。

151
00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:19.230
But it is funny because the character of Angela is not always nice.
但这也挺逗的，因为安吉拉这个角色并不总是那么讨人喜欢。

152
00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:25.010
So I walked into it with some trepidation, and then I had to remind myself, oh, right, these people are just really good at what they do.
所以我走进去的时候还有点忐忑，然后我不得不提醒自己，哦，对哦，这些人只是非常擅长他们的工作。

153
00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:32.390
Like, I'm acting with Angela and Rain, that is different than, quote, Angela and Dwight.
比如说，我在和安吉拉和雷恩对戏，这跟所谓的“安吉拉和德怀特”是不一样的。

154
00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:39.210
And it was that funny thing to walk onto a set, and I had been on enough sets before that I should not have fallen for that.
那种走进片场的感觉挺奇妙的，而且我以前去过足够多的片场，本来不该被这种表象给糊弄过去的。

155
00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:51.710
But it just tells you how much the characters of The Office seeped into our consciousness in a way that was very real and organic and genuine and where people bought it.
但这也说明了《办公室》里的角色已经多么深入我们的潜意识，以一种非常真实、自然、地道且让人深信不疑的方式。

156
00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:55.710
Because even I, someone in comedy, was like, oh, right, these people are nice.
因为连我这个身处喜剧界的人都觉得，哦，对哦，这些人其实人很好。

157
00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:56.850
They're not the characters.
他们可不是剧里的角色。

158
00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:08.350
So I remember being so acutely aware that we were shooting inside a minivan, and you two knew each other so well, and neither of you knew me.
所以我记得当时特别清晰地意识到，我们是在一辆面包车里拍摄，你们俩对彼此那么熟悉，而你们俩都不认识我。

159
00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:16.370
So to be in a social environment where not just while shooting but in between takes, we're all just sitting in a minivan together,
所以处在这样一个社交环境中，不仅是在拍摄期间，甚至在拍片间隙，我们大家就一起挤在一辆面包车里，

160
00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:26.250
and you guys have, like, you know, a decade of intimate knowledge of how each other's lives work and things to chit-chat about and small talk.
而你们俩，你知道的，对彼此的生活了解了整整十年，有很多可以闲聊和寒暄的话题。

161
00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:28.170
And then I'm also just some guy.
然后我呢，也只是个无名小卒。

162
00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:31.950
I remember that being very funny to me and leading to some giggling.
我记得这对我来说特别搞笑，还引发了一阵傻笑。

163
00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.170
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

164
00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.670
I love all of that.
我太喜欢这些了。

165
00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:36.190
I know.
我也知道。

166
00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:44.190
So, I mean, Chris was so lovely, and I just remember him falling right into step right away.
所以，我的意思是，克里斯非常可爱，我只记得他马上就进入了状态。

167
00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:48.090
And I also remember that Rain was so enamored with him.
而且我还记得雷恩非常迷恋他。

168
00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.570
Rain was so tickled by him.
雷恩被他逗得乐不可支。

169
00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.050
Everything he said, Rain would just get the giggles.
他说的每一句话，都能让雷恩咯咯直笑。

170
00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.030
And it was really fun.
真的很有趣。

171
00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:55.930
It was a fun day.
那是个愉快的一天。

172
00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.170
Aw, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

173
00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.510
I'm sure you're going to have more stories as we break down the episode.
我相信在我们剖析这集的时候，你还会有更多故事要讲。

174
00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:00.050
Oh, I do.
噢，我确实有。

175
00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:06.630
All right, fast fact number two, I'm calling it The Reviews Are In.
好了，速报第二条，我给它起名叫“评论出炉”。

176
00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.790
Oh, your fast fact has a title.
哇，你的速报居然还有标题。

177
00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:09.750
I titled it.
我给它起的名。

178
00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:10.050
Okay.
好吧。

179
00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.430
We said we loved this episode.
我们说过我们很喜欢这一集。

180
00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.190
The reviewers agreed.
评论家们也这么认为。

181
00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.730
It was a hit.
这是一部大热之作。

182
00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:24.190
But there was one thing in particular that was cited in every single review, and Angela Kinsey, it was you.
但有一点特别之处在每一篇评论中都被提及了，安吉拉·金斯利，那就是你。

183
00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:24.990
Oh, come on.
哦，拜托。

184
00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.050
Your performance.
你的表演。

185
00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:30.410
And by the way, I love your performance in this episode so much.
顺便说一句，我真的太喜欢你在这集里的表演了。

186
00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:30.950
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

187
00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.450
So much, Angela.
太喜欢了，安吉拉。

188
00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:37.810
And so it made me very excited to read all these reviews about your performance, and here they are.
所以读到所有这些赞美你演技的评论时，我感到非常兴奋，它们在这里。

189
00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:47.710
Eric Adams, he was the new reviewer at AV Club, gave this episode an A- and said it was your plotline with Oscar that was a season highlight.
埃里克·亚当斯，他是AV Club的新评论员，给这一集打出了A-的高分，并表示你和奥斯卡的剧情线是这一季的亮点。

190
00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:48.890
That's a quote.
原话如此。

191
00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:53.570
And he complimented you in particular for your commitment to character.
而且他特别称赞了你对角色的投入。

192
00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.250
Thank you.
谢谢。

193
00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:56.590
That's not all.
还不止这些呢。

194
00:09:56.850 --> 00:10:00.270
The Paste writer called it your best performance of the year.
《Paste》杂志的撰稿人称这是你今年最好的表演。

195
00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:01.050
Wow.
哇。

196
00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:01.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

197
00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.270
Michael Tedder praised the writers for giving your character a chance to shine.
迈克尔·泰德赞扬了编剧们给了你的角色一个大放异彩的机会。

198
00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:12.730
And this was also rated the fifth best episode of the season, according to fans on Office Tally.
根据Office Tally上粉丝们的投票，这也获评为本季第五佳的一集。

199
00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:15.890
And again, the comments cited you.
而且评论里又一次提到了你。

200
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.150
You an Oscar, but you, lady.
你和奥斯卡，不过重点是你，这位女士。

201
00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:19.810
Star of the episode.
本集之星。

202
00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.390
I don't even know what to say.
我简直不知道该说什么好。

203
00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.830
That makes me—that just warms my heart.
这让我——这真的让我心里暖洋洋的。

204
00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:33.470
You know, when you're part of a show like The Office and there's such a deep cast of amazing people, when you're a supporting actor,
你知道的，当你参演像《办公室》这样一部演员阵容极其深厚且优秀的剧集时，作为一个配角，

205
00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:38.530
you just have to be patient and hope that someday you get your turn.
你只能保持耐心，期望有一天能轮到你出彩。

206
00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.710
And Kate Flannery and I used to talk a lot about that.
我和凯特·弗兰纳里以前经常聊起这个。

207
00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.810
You know, she would say, Ange, we're not the meat, we're the seasoning.
你知道的，她会说，安吉，我们不是主菜，我们是调味料。

208
00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.410
But the seasoning has their day.
但调味料也有出头之日。

209
00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:48.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

210
00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:51.970
And I was so, so delighted by the storyline.
我对这个故事线感到非常、非常的开心。

211
00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.390
And I have such fond memories of getting to do it.
而且我对拍摄这段经历有着非常美好的回忆。

212
00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.590
Well, lady, if you thought I was finished, I'm not.
好了，女士，如果你以为我说完了，那可没有。

213
00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:57.590
There's more of this fast fact.
这则幕后快讯还有更多内容。

214
00:10:57.770 --> 00:10:58.250
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

215
00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:58.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

216
00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:04.150
In addition to reaching out to Chris Gethard, we also reached out to the director of this episode, Brent Forrester.
除了联系克里斯·盖瑟德，我们还联系了本集的导演布伦特·福斯特。

217
00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.310
And I have an audio clip from Brent just for you.
我这里有一段布伦特专门发给你的音频。

218
00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:07.810
Oh.
哦。

219
00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:14.750
Jenna, you mentioned that when you rewatched this episode, you were struck by how grounded the performances of the actors are.
珍娜，你提到当你重看这一集时，演员们的表演之扎实让你印象深刻。

220
00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:24.450
And I actually believe that the actors saved this episode because the premise is potentially so crazy, especially for a show like The Office,
而且我实际上相信是演员们拯救了这一集，因为这个设定本身可能太疯狂了，特别是对于《办公室》这样一部剧来说，

221
00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:30.270
which is famous for having the most realistic tone of any show in the history of network TV.
它以拥有电视网历史上所有剧集中最写实的基调而闻名。

222
00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:35.870
How do we get away with an episode in which one of the characters is threatening to assassinate the other character in the office?
我们怎么能拍这样一集：其中一个角色在办公室里威胁要暗杀另一个角色？

223
00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.850
Well, the answer is the performances of the actors.
好吧，答案就是演员们的表演。

224
00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:52.510
Somehow, Rain, Oscar, and especially Angela managed to find some kind of emotional reality in the performances that ends up redeeming this zany premise.
不知何故，雷恩、奥斯卡，尤其是安吉拉，设法在表演中找到了一种情感上的真实感，最终挽救了这个滑稽的设定。

225
00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:58.650
So that at the end, after all this frenetic activity, when Angela says to Oscar, you were supposed to be my friend,
所以在最后，在经历了一系列狂热的活动之后，当安吉拉对奥斯卡说，你本该是我的朋友时，

226
00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:03.650
there's a feeling of real emotional tenderness there within this crazy setting.
在这个疯狂的环境中，有一种真实的情感温柔感。

227
00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.810
I don't know how they did it.
我不知道他们是怎么做到的。

228
00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:09.030
And I wish you would ask Angela how she pulled this off.
我希望你问问安吉拉她是怎么办到的。

229
00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:13.330
I think that's a really good analysis of why this episode works.
我认为这是对为什么这一集能成功的一个非常好的分析。

230
00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.530
Angela, how'd you pull it off?
安吉拉，你是怎么办到的？

231
00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.050
Gosh, that's such a big question.
天哪，这是一个好大的问题。

232
00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.290
Well, Brent, thank you so much.
好的，布伦特，非常感谢你。

233
00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.550
You're always so generous and kind.
你总是这么慷慨和善良。

234
00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.750
Really, Angela Martin was a real person to me.
真的，对我来说安吉拉·马丁是一个活生生的人。

235
00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:29.750
She was.
她的确是。

236
00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:42.270
So I had to think about her life and how she tried so hard to have this persona and image of the senator's wife and what that meant to her.
所以我不得不思考她的生活，思考她是如何极力维持参议员夫人的人设和形象的，以及这对她意味着什么。

237
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.650
That status meant so much to her.
这种地位对她来说太重要了。

238
00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:58.610
And when Oscar has this affair, someone who she trusts, who she has sat next to for years and years and years, that threatens everything about who she thought she was,
当奥斯卡搞外遇时，这个她信任的人、这个与她并肩坐了多年的人，威胁到了她对自己身份认同的一切认知，

239
00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.350
this image that she puts out to the world.
也就是她向世界展现的这个形象。

240
00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.130
It was all shattered.
这一切都粉碎了。

241
00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.350
And she probably went to a pretty dark place.
她可能经历了一段相当黑暗的时期。

242
00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:10.430
And Angela's dark place was, I'm going to mess you up.
而安吉拉黑暗的一面就是，我要整死你。

243
00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:11.170
You know?
你知道吗？

244
00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:16.870
But I never thought that she wanted Oscar to be seriously injured.
但我从没想过她是真的想让奥斯卡受到严重伤害。

245
00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:21.750
I think she just wanted to scare him and let him know how pissed off she was.
我觉得她只是想吓唬他一下，让他知道她有多生气。

246
00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:25.250
That was sort of how I approached it.
这就是我处理这个角色的大致方式。

247
00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.270
She was just hurt.
她只是受伤了。

248
00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.550
She was really hurt.
她是真的很受伤。

249
00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:36.810
I mean, I think everything you just said is so emotional and real and grounded and relatable.
我是说，我觉得你刚刚说的所有这些都充满情感、真实、扎实且引人共鸣。

250
00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:44.290
And that is why this premise doesn't get zany, because you grounded it in all that realness.
这就是为什么这个设定不会显得滑稽，因为你把它建立在所有这些真实感之上。

251
00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:48.670
You know, it was really hard, though, because I wanted to jump in and be silly, but I couldn't.
你知道的，不过这其实真的很难，因为我想加入进去一起胡闹，但我不能。

252
00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:53.230
Like, we'll get to it, but the scene in the van with the receipts, oh, my gosh.
比如，我们待会儿会聊到，但那场在面包车里看收据的戏，哦，天哪。

253
00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:53.850
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

254
00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:56.790
But I had to play it as honest as I could.
但我必须尽可能真实地去演绎她。

255
00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:57.270
Yeah.
是啊。

256
00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:04.430
Even though there was a little bit of zany happening around her, she was still very hurt and angry.
尽管她身边发生了一些疯狂搞笑的事，但她当时依然非常受伤和生气。

257
00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:07.130
Those were real emotions, so I had to play them real.
那些都是真实的感情，所以我必须真实地演出来。

258
00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:08.650
I just loved it so much.
我真的是太喜欢了。

259
00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:09.370
Thanks, lady.
谢谢你，女士。

260
00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:10.290
Thanks, everybody.
谢谢大家。

261
00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:11.350
All right.
好的。

262
00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.550
Moving on to fast fact number three.
接下来进入第三个速报冷知识。

263
00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:19.090
Angela, last week you had a mailbag moment, which I loved.
安吉拉，上周你有一个听众来信环节，我可太喜欢了。

264
00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:23.130
And I thought I might like to have a mailbag moment this week.
然后我想我这周兴许也想来个听众来信环节。

265
00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:23.570
Okay.
好呀。

266
00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.650
So this will be a mailbag moment with Jenna.
所以这将是珍娜的听众来信时间。

267
00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:32.410
This is a post that I was made aware of that was on the Office Ladies' Facebook fan page.
这是一篇别人转告给我的帖子，发在《办公室女士》的Facebook粉丝专页上。

268
00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:39.330
It's from a poster named Chris C., and it was posted after we broke down the episode Welcome Party.
发帖人叫克里斯·C，这是在我们详细解析了《欢迎派对》那一集之后发的。

269
00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:46.450
That's the one where Andy and Erin are driving back from Florida together, and they decide to stop at Jessica's parents' cabin.
就是安迪和艾琳从佛罗里达一起开车回来，决定顺道去杰西卡父母的小木屋那一集。

270
00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.570
Yes, at what was like a bachelorette party.
对，就是那个类似于单身单身派对的地方。

271
00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:50.210
Yes.
对。

272
00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:50.890
Okay.
好。

273
00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:54.190
Here is what Chris posted after that episode.
以下是克里斯看完那一集后发的贴。

274
00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:59.890
I had a good laugh at this week's podcast regarding the penis cake and gummy straws.
对于本周播客里聊到的那个阴茎蛋糕和软糖吸管，我笑了好久。

275
00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:02.610
Remember we had that big conversation?
还记得我们当时进行了那么长时间的讨论吗？

276
00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:03.150
Yes.
记得。

277
00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:11.010
Chris said, I have a ladies group, and each month one of us hosts a night for just us ladies and some drinks.
