00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.180
I remember this.
我记得这个。

446
00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.640
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

447
00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.420
And then it says, the staff all applauds itself.
接着上面写着，全体员工为自己鼓掌。

448
00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:41.300
We're very pleased with what we've donated.
我们对我们捐赠的东西非常满意。

449
00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:45.540
But then Daryl starts looking at what all the people brought in to donate.
但接着达里尔开始查看大家带来捐赠的东西。

450
00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:47.060
It is so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

451
00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.560
He starts calling people out.
他开始点名批评大家了。

452
00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.820
He's like, Phyllis, you brought in water chestnuts.
他说，菲利斯，你带了马蹄（荸荠）。

453
00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:53.720
Meredith also water chestnuts.
梅雷迪思带的也是马蹄。

454
00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:57.540
Creed brought in a can of garbanzo beans dated 1990.
克里德带了一罐保质期到1990年的鹰嘴豆。

455
00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.240
Someone else brought in racquetballs.
还有人带了壁球。

456
00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.440
And Daryl is getting so annoyed.
达瑞尔变得非常恼火。

457
00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:05.740
Then he holds up a can and says, I don't even know what this is.
然后他举起一个罐头说，我甚至不知道这是什么。

458
00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:07.560
And Kevin says, it's brown.
凯文说，它是棕色的。

459
00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:09.540
And Daryl's like, what?
达瑞尔说，什么？

460
00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:13.980
Kevin then has a talking head where he says, I eat brown every week.
接着凯文有一段对着镜头的采访，他说，我每周都吃棕色食物。

461
00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:16.680
Hot brown, ice brown, scrambled brown.
热的棕色，冰的棕色，炒的棕色。

462
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:19.340
And then he holds up a can that has a little pig on it.
然后他举起一个印有小猪图案的罐头。

463
00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:22.300
And in Russian, it says dog food.
上面用俄语写着狗粮。

464
00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:23.060
Yes.
是的。

465
00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.980
I so remember this.
我太记得这个了。

466
00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:27.080
And then Toby gets upset.
然后托比不高兴了。

467
00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:27.940
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

468
00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:31.760
But I have a solution for your poor participation in this canned food drive.
但对于你们这次罐头食品募捐活动的不积极参与，我有一个解决方案。

469
00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:36.700
Instead of going home early today, we'll be having a little Thanksgiving feast of our own
今天我们不提前回家了，我们要举办一个属于我们自己的小型感恩节盛宴

470
00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.820
made with your canned food.
用你们捐的罐头食品来做。

471
00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.300
And Kevin at first was like, yes.
凯文起初还觉得，太好了。

472
00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:45.040
And then when Toby says with your canned food, Kevin goes, you son of a bitch.
然后当托比说“用你们的罐头食品”时，凯文说，你这个王八蛋。

473
00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:51.820
Then there's a whole montage of the Dunder Mifflin crew making this Thanksgiving lunch out
接着是一组邓德米夫林员工用这些糟糕的罐头捐赠

474
00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:53.680
of these lame canned contributions.
来制作这个感恩节午餐的剪辑镜头。

475
00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.760
And here's how the scene ends.
场景是这样结束的。

476
00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:56.680
I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听看。

477
00:22:57.380 --> 00:22:58.280
Happy Thanksgiving.
感恩节快乐。

478
00:22:58.720 --> 00:23:01.320
And remember, you did this to yourselves.
记住，这是你们自找的。

479
00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.120
I think everybody learned a valuable lesson.
我想每个人都学到了宝贵的一课。

480
00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:12.340
And if I had a Thanksgiving meal with other people for the first time in years, good for me.
如果我多年来第一次和别人一起吃感恩节大餐，那也是我应得的。

481
00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:14.320
Aw, Toby.
哦，托比。

482
00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:18.960
So we did have a Thanksgiving episode.
所以我们确实拍过一集感恩节主题。

483
00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:20.180
This would have been it.
本来就是这一集。

484
00:23:20.180 --> 00:23:24.080
But wow, our only nod to Thanksgiving and it got cut out.
但哇，我们唯一向感恩节致敬的片段居然被剪掉了。

485
00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:24.680
That's right.
没错。

486
00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:29.380
Well, I think there was just too much good stuff in this episode.
嗯，我觉得这集里精彩的内容实在太多了。

487
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:30.000
Yeah.
对啊。

488
00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:32.320
That we just didn't have room for a cold open.
以至于我们根本没有空间放片头前戏了。

489
00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:33.800
We start right with the plot.
我们直接切入剧情。

490
00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:34.380
Yep.
没错。

491
00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.440
But there's a bunch in deleted scenes.
但删减片段里有很多内容。

492
00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.400
So if you have the DVDs, you can go watch them.
所以如果你有DVD，你可以去看那些片段。

493
00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:41.260
Well, now Pam and Jim are going to arrive to the office.
好了，现在帕姆和吉姆要到办公室了。

494
00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:46.840
And Pam is wearing her painting clothes because she's going to finally start on the mural in the
帕姆穿着她画画时穿的衣服，因为她终于要开始画仓库里的

495
00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:47.360
warehouse.
壁画了。

496
00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:50.840
Meredith has such sidebar sass.
梅雷迪思真是太会冷嘲热讽了。

497
00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:53.280
She goes, queen of the primer, this one.
她说，底漆女王，就是这位。

498
00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:54.040
Yeah.
对。

499
00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:57.120
She asked Pam, you sure you don't want to put another coat of primer on it?
她问帕姆，你确定不再刷一层底漆吗？

500
00:23:57.740 --> 00:23:58.760
Queen of the primer.
底漆女王。

501
00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:01.380
We had a fan question from Colleen S.
我们收到了来自芝加哥的柯琳·S. 的粉丝提问，

502
00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.120
in Chicago who said,
她说：

503
00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:06.060
Do you have any stories behind Pam's painting clothes?
“你们有什么关于潘的画画衣服背后的故事吗？”

504
00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:10.700
The outfit was auctioned off after the series ended and I ended up winning it.
那套衣服在剧集结束后被拿去拍卖了，最后我把它拍了下来。

505
00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.660
Jenna, if you would like to have it back, I would be more than happy to send it to you.
珍娜，如果你想要回它的话，我很乐意把它寄给你。

506
00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:16.900
Colleen, I have to tell you something.
柯琳，我得告诉你一件事。

507
00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.620
I have one too.
我也有一个。

508
00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:20.440
There were multiples.
有好几套呢。

509
00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:23.920
You know, all of our outfits, we had more than one.
你知道的，我们所有的戏服都不止一套。

510
00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:27.480
We had doubles in case we spilled something on it or something happened.
我们有备用装，以防把东西洒在上面或者发生什么意外。

511
00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:31.380
So I have one of the sweatshirts and you must have the other one.
所以我也有一件卫衣，你那件一定就是另外一件了。

512
00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.880
So I have one of the Pratt sweatshirts with all the paint on it.
所以我也有一件印满颜料的普瑞特学院卫衣。

513
00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:39.360
And this was just the idea of Alicia Raycraft, our costume designer.
这只是我们的服装设计师艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫的想法。

514
00:24:39.360 --> 00:24:42.700
She came and she said, What do you think Pam's painting clothes are?
她走过来说：“你们觉得潘的画画衣服应该是什么样的？”

515
00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:43.860
And she had this idea.
然后她就有了这个想法。

516
00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:47.600
And I loved this callback to her time at Pratt.
我特别喜欢这个对她在普瑞特求学时光的呼应。

517
00:24:47.740 --> 00:24:49.400
I just absolutely loved it.
我真的超级喜欢。

518
00:24:49.640 --> 00:24:50.500
So creative.
太有创意了。

519
00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:53.000
It also looks like a very cozy sweatshirt.
而且看起来也是一件很舒服的卫衣。

520
00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:54.320
Oh, I loved this outfit.
哦，我超爱这套衣服。

521
00:24:54.520 --> 00:24:54.940
I bet.
我敢说。

522
00:24:55.140 --> 00:24:56.040
You got to wear jeans.
你终于能穿牛仔裤了。

523
00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:56.660
Jeans.
牛仔裤。

524
00:24:56.820 --> 00:24:58.960
I can't believe you wore pantyhose for nine years.
真不敢相信你穿了九年的连裤袜。

525
00:24:59.100 --> 00:24:59.340
I know.
就是说啊。

526
00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:01.820
I didn't wear them one day.
我有一天没穿。

527
00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:03.980
Every time you say it, it hurts me.
你每次说起这个，我都觉得心痛。

528
00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:09.540
I just shoved them aside and no one said anything.
我只是把它们扒到一边，根本没人说什么。

529
00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:10.160
I don't know.
我不知道。

530
00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:11.060
I'm a rule follower.
我是个循规蹈矩的人。

531
00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:11.540
You are.
你确实是。

532
00:25:12.100 --> 00:25:14.680
Jim and Pam are now going to have a joint talking head.
吉姆和潘现在要有一个双人访谈了。

533
00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:20.000
And Jim explains that he has to ask David Wallace if he can start working part time
吉姆解释说他必须去问大卫·华莱士是否可以开始兼职，

534
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:23.120
because his sports marketing team really needs him.
因为他的体育营销团队真的很需要他。

535
00:25:23.440 --> 00:25:27.400
He also shares in his absence, they named the company Athlete.
他还分享说在他不在的时候，他们把公司命名为了“运动员”。

536
00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:28.900
While he wasn't there.
就在他不在场的时候。

537
00:25:29.020 --> 00:25:29.200
Yeah.
是啊。

538
00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:31.660
He was like, I could have prevented that if I had been there.
他的感觉就像是：我要是在场的话，就能阻止这件事了。

539
00:25:31.980 --> 00:25:32.220
Yep.
没错。

540
00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:34.000
I guess Jim doesn't like the name.
我猜吉姆不喜欢这个名字。

541
00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.340
I like Athlete.
我觉得“运动员”挺好的。

542
00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:35.800
I don't.
我不觉得。

543
00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:36.700
I think it's terrible.
我觉得这名字太糟了。

544
00:25:36.820 --> 00:25:37.240
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

545
00:25:38.100 --> 00:25:42.160
It's like so, it's so well chosen that it's a bad name.
它的感觉就是，选得太刻意了反而成了一个烂名字。

546
00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:44.480
It's hard to say Athlete.
“运动员”这词很难念。

547
00:25:44.840 --> 00:25:45.640
I don't like it.
我不喜欢。

548
00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:46.080
Athlete.
运动员。

549
00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:48.080
Sounds like athlete's foot to me.
听起来就像脚气一样。

550
00:25:48.280 --> 00:25:48.800
I don't know.
我不知道。

551
00:25:48.940 --> 00:25:49.620
But then it's elite.
但那样的话就很精英了。

552
00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:50.700
I don't get it.
我不明白。

553
00:25:50.820 --> 00:25:52.100
I don't like the play on words.
我不喜欢这个双关语。

554
00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:57.340
We had a fan question from Chaley D in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, who said,
我们收到了来自宾夕法尼亚州匹兹堡的查利·D的粉丝提问，他说：

555
00:25:57.460 --> 00:26:00.880
were there any other ideas for the name of the company?
公司名字还有过其他备选吗？

556
00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:02.520
There must have been so many.
肯定有很多吧。

557
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:03.700
I asked Brent.
我问过布伦特了。

558
00:26:04.120 --> 00:26:06.040
He said there were so many names.
他说有很多名字。

559
00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:09.420
He said writers love riffing on dumb names.
他说编剧们就喜欢拿蠢名字开涮。

560
00:26:09.580 --> 00:26:10.960
And here are a few.
这里有几个。

561
00:26:11.840 --> 00:26:12.320
Winnovate.
赢新特。

562
00:26:12.840 --> 00:26:13.320
Okay.
好吧。

563
00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:15.000
Champlify.
畅普莱费.

564
00:26:16.760 --> 00:26:17.460
That's funny.
真搞笑。

565
00:26:17.980 --> 00:26:20.420
And, gosh, I don't even know how to say this one.
天哪，我都不知道这个该怎么念。

566
00:26:21.380 --> 00:26:21.860
Jockatagon.
Jockatagon。

567
00:26:22.300 --> 00:26:22.640
What?
什么？

568
00:26:22.780 --> 00:26:23.440
Can I see it?
我能看看吗？

569
00:26:23.580 --> 00:26:26.100
Yeah, I think it's like octagon, but it's joctagon.
对，我觉得就像八边形（octagon），但它是joctagon。

570
00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:27.420
Like a jockstrap?
就像运动护裆吗？

571
00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:28.080
I don't know.
我不知道。

572
00:26:28.240 --> 00:26:29.580
I think like jock, like athlete.
我觉得像是jock，也就是运动员的意思。

573
00:26:29.700 --> 00:26:30.540
Oh, like an athlete.
哦，就像运动员一样。

574
00:26:30.760 --> 00:26:31.500
Jock to Vaughn.
Jock to Vaughn。

575
00:26:31.920 --> 00:26:33.180
There's no V in it, lady.
里面没有V字母，大姐。

576
00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:34.160
It's joctagon.
它是joctagon。

577
00:26:34.580 --> 00:26:35.580
Oh, joctagon.
哦，joctagon。

578
00:26:35.820 --> 00:26:36.060
Yeah.
对。

579
00:26:36.640 --> 00:26:38.240
Did I say Vaughn every time?
我刚才每次都念成Vaughn了吗？

580
00:26:38.500 --> 00:26:39.620
That last time you did.
你刚才最后一次是那样。

581
00:26:39.820 --> 00:26:41.080
Yeah, I did the last time.
对，我最后一次那样念了。

582
00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.020
Joctagon, like octagon.
Joctagon，就像八边形一样。

583
00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:43.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

584
00:26:43.700 --> 00:26:43.920
Yeah.
对。

585
00:26:44.220 --> 00:26:45.500
I like Champlify.
我挺喜欢Champlify的。

586
00:26:45.780 --> 00:26:50.180
That, to me, would have hit the joke harder than athlete, but maybe it's too ridiculous.
在我看来，这个笑话的效果会比athlete更强烈，不过可能太荒谬了。

587
00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:52.500
Well, athlete is a better name than Champlify.
好吧，athlete比Champlify是个更好的名字。

588
00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:53.520
Yeah.
对。

589
00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:55.640
But Champlify is very funny to say.
但Champlify念起来太好玩了。

590
00:26:55.880 --> 00:26:56.360
It is.
确实。

591
00:26:56.880 --> 00:27:00.020
Lady, I have a tangent that just popped into my head.
大姐，我脑子里突然冒出一个题外话。

592
00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:02.220
It is in no way related to this episode.
它跟这一集一点关系都没有。

593
00:27:02.420 --> 00:27:04.920
In fact, it's related to an episode of The Crown.
事实上，它跟《王冠》的一集有关。

594
00:27:05.120 --> 00:27:05.920
Oh, I'm taking—
哦，我要—

595
00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:06.100
Do you mind?
你介意吗？

596
00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:07.420
I don't—are you kidding?
我才不—你开玩笑吧？

597
00:27:07.420 --> 00:27:07.920
The Crown?
《王冠》？

598
00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:08.640
I don't mind.
我不介意。

599
00:27:08.780 --> 00:27:09.760
I'm taking off my glasses.
我要摘下眼镜了。

600
00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:10.880
I'm getting my cup of tea.
我去拿杯茶。

601
00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:11.520
Let's hear it.
听听看吧。

602
00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:13.180
Okay, this is totally unplanned.
好吧，这完全是个突发奇想。

603
00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:13.560
Okay.
好的。

604
00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:15.100
It's not in my document.
这不在我的稿子里。

605
00:27:15.280 --> 00:27:16.140
I know it's not.
我知道不在。

606
00:27:16.300 --> 00:27:16.580
Okay.
好吧。

607
00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:22.180
The other night, Lee and I were watching The Crown, the latest season, the final season.
前几天晚上，我和李在看《王冠》，最新的一季，最后一季。

608
00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:22.500
Yeah.
对。

609
00:27:22.500 --> 00:27:25.980
And I'm on the episode where Prince William has gone to college.
然后我看到威廉王子上大学的那一集。

610
00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:26.500
Yes.
对。

611
00:27:26.680 --> 00:27:29.520
And he goes out to a party one night, and they do beer bongs.
有一天晚上他去参加派对，然后他们玩了漏斗灌酒。

612
00:27:30.020 --> 00:27:30.180
Yeah.
对。

613
00:27:30.680 --> 00:27:32.240
Have you ever done a beer bong?
你玩过漏斗灌酒吗？

614
00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:33.580
