德怀特说，不行，你已经失去了这种特权。

777
00:34:05.890 --> 00:34:08.690
If I'm not in your panties, I don't go vigilantes.
我都进不了你的内裤，休想让我当法外狂徒。

778
00:34:09.390 --> 00:34:10.470
You've got to know.
你得清楚。

779
00:34:11.030 --> 00:34:15.170
Some writer pitched that, and when it made it in, it was just, like, so tickled.
某个编剧想出了这句词，当它被采用时，大家简直乐坏了。

780
00:34:15.490 --> 00:34:17.050
Yes, we should have asked Brent about that.
是的，我们早该问问布伦特的。

781
00:34:17.150 --> 00:34:18.310
That's a really funny line.
这台词真逗。

782
00:34:18.450 --> 00:34:18.990
It is.
确实。

783
00:34:19.710 --> 00:34:23.290
Angela then confesses to Dwight that her marriage is in danger.
安吉拉随后向德怀特坦白，她的婚姻亮起了红灯。

784
00:34:23.430 --> 00:34:25.030
She doesn't know who she can truSt.
她不知道该信任谁。

785
00:34:25.570 --> 00:34:29.950
Dwight says, you know, I know just the guy, the former cop who was kicked off the force.
德怀特说，你知道的，我正认识这么个人，那个被警队开除的前警察。

786
00:34:30.370 --> 00:34:34.250
And then he says, I'm going to SMS text him to set up a meeting.
然后他说，我要发短信联系他安排见面。

787
00:34:34.690 --> 00:34:35.790
Gets back to him right away.
立刻就回复了他。

788
00:34:35.790 --> 00:34:36.450
Okay, no problem.
行，没问题。

789
00:34:36.590 --> 00:34:37.190
He's free anytime.
他随时都有空。

790
00:34:37.470 --> 00:34:37.730
Yeah.
对。

791
00:34:39.210 --> 00:34:42.110
Well, now Jim is on the phone with David Wallace.
好吧，现在吉姆在和大卫·华莱士通电话。

792
00:34:42.710 --> 00:34:49.350
He's doing this phone call at his desk because Jim doesn't know how to make phone calls more private.
他在办公桌前打这通电话，因为吉姆不知道怎么让通话更私密一点。

793
00:34:49.590 --> 00:34:50.450
No, he doesn't.
不，他确实不知道。

794
00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:50.700
We learned that.
我们见识过了。

795
00:34:50.890 --> 00:34:53.110
No, he's not going to have a private conversation.
不，他根本不会去进行私密对话。

796
00:34:53.390 --> 00:34:57.830
And Jim is like, listen, it'll just be a couple days a week that I would be in Philly.
吉姆说，听着，我一周只需要去费城几天。

797
00:34:58.090 --> 00:34:59.870
I'd be in Scranton the other days.
其他日子我会在斯克兰顿。

798
00:34:59.870 --> 00:35:01.830
And, you know, what do you think?
而且，你觉得怎么样？

799
00:35:01.970 --> 00:35:04.470
And David Wallace is kind of like, I don't know, Jim.
大卫·华莱士的反应有点像，我不知道，吉姆。

800
00:35:04.470 --> 00:35:06.630
It kind of seems like, what if something goes down?
总觉得有点，万一出了什么事怎么办？

801
00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:08.930
I need someone there in person to deal with it.
我需要有人亲自去处理这件事。

802
00:35:10.310 --> 00:35:11.650
So Jim lies.
所以吉姆撒谎了。

803
00:35:12.010 --> 00:35:15.870
In the moment, he says, oh, Phyllis and Stanley offered to cover for me.
当时他说，哦，菲莉丝和斯坦利答应帮我顶班。

804
00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:18.230
And David's like, oh, well, if that's the case, okay.
然后大卫就说，哦，好吧，既然这样，那就行。

805
00:35:19.230 --> 00:35:24.930
I will point out, I think David Wallace might be the most lax boss ever.
我要指出的是，我觉得大卫·华莱士可能是有史以来最散漫的老板。

806
00:35:25.230 --> 00:35:25.570
Yeah.
确实。

807
00:35:25.890 --> 00:35:26.910
And he's off on a boat.
而且他跑去划船了。

808
00:35:27.090 --> 00:35:27.810
No problem.
没问题。

809
00:35:28.190 --> 00:35:31.170
Jim's like, I want to only be part-time but pay me the same.
吉姆说，我想只做兼职但拿全职薪水。

810
00:35:31.170 --> 00:35:32.090
He's like, okay.
他说，好吧。

811
00:35:32.890 --> 00:35:33.370
Yeah.
是啊。

812
00:35:33.750 --> 00:35:35.410
We should all work for David Wallace.
我们都该给大卫·华莱士打工。

813
00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:36.150
No kidding.
可不是嘛。

814
00:35:36.530 --> 00:35:42.670
We had a fan question from Emily J in Ohio who said, is Pam not a salesman at all anymore?
我们收到了俄亥俄州艾米莉·J发来的粉丝提问，她问，潘现在完全不是销售了吗？

815
00:35:43.190 --> 00:35:45.570
Why does Jim need Phyllis and Stanley to cover?
为什么吉姆需要菲莉丝和斯坦利来顶班？

816
00:35:45.710 --> 00:35:46.670
Can't Pam cover?
潘不能顶班吗？

817
00:35:47.210 --> 00:35:48.450
Emily made a good point.
艾米莉问得很好。

818
00:35:48.610 --> 00:35:52.690
I think I'm trying to remember back when Pam became the office administrator.
我想我在回想潘成为办公室行政主管的时候。

819
00:35:53.310 --> 00:35:57.450
I think she was still going to keep her couple of clients that she had.
我觉得她当时还是打算保留她原有的几个客户。

820
00:35:57.650 --> 00:35:59.410
She still does a little sales, right?
她现在还是做一点销售，对吧？

821
00:36:00.130 --> 00:36:01.590
Oh, I thought she was done.
哦，我以为她不做了。

822
00:36:01.770 --> 00:36:05.510
I thought she created a new position and she was no longer part of the sales team.
我以为她创造了一个新职位，不再是销售团队的一员了。

823
00:36:05.650 --> 00:36:06.770
That's how I saw it.
我是这么看的。

824
00:36:06.930 --> 00:36:07.930
I couldn't remember.
我记不清了。

825
00:36:08.310 --> 00:36:13.830
But let's say, like, sure, she does still do a little bit of sales.
但假设，比如说，她确实还做一点点销售。

826
00:36:14.090 --> 00:36:17.130
I think the question is, do you want Pam covering for you?
我觉得问题是，你想让潘帮你顶班吗？

827
00:36:17.390 --> 00:36:19.190
She was the worst salesperson.
她可是最差的销售员。

828
00:36:19.190 --> 00:36:24.450
I'm not sure David Wallace is going to let Jim go to Philly a couple days a week if the
我不确定大卫·华莱士是否会同意吉姆一周去费城几天，如果

829
00:36:24.450 --> 00:36:25.290
backup is Pam.
备用人选是潘的话。

830
00:36:26.070 --> 00:36:26.910
I don't know.
我不知道。

831
00:36:27.070 --> 00:36:30.970
I'm just saying, you know, no offense to Pam, but like this is-
我只是说，你知道的，无意冒犯潘，但这就——

832
00:36:30.970 --> 00:36:31.830
Sales are not her thing.
销售不是她的强项。

833
00:36:31.950 --> 00:36:33.030
Sales were not her thing.
销售过去不是她的强项。

834
00:36:33.150 --> 00:36:35.170
We don't have to all be good at everything all the time.
我们没必要每时每刻在每件事上都表现得很好。

835
00:36:35.310 --> 00:36:35.750
No, we don't.
不，没必要。

836
00:36:35.890 --> 00:36:36.210
It's okay, Pam.
没关系的，潘。

837
00:36:36.390 --> 00:36:36.590
Yeah.
对。

838
00:36:36.710 --> 00:36:37.310
We love you.
我们爱你。

839
00:36:37.750 --> 00:36:39.510
Well, now we go back to the break room.
好吧，现在我们回到休息室。

840
00:36:39.770 --> 00:36:44.130
Stanley and Phyllis are there and Jim comes in and really wants them to help him.
斯坦利和菲莉丝在那里，吉姆进来，非常希望他们能帮他。

841
00:36:44.430 --> 00:36:46.270
He says, hey, we're friends, right?
他说，嘿，我们是朋友，对吧？

842
00:36:46.550 --> 00:36:48.310
And Stanley's like, we're not friends.
然后斯坦利说，我们不是朋友。

843
00:36:48.310 --> 00:36:52.030
Yeah, Stanley's like, if we were friends, when's my birthday, Jim?
对，斯坦利说，如果我们是朋友，我生日是什么时候，吉姆？

844
00:36:52.230 --> 00:36:54.490
And Jim is like, when's my birthday?
然后吉姆就说，我生日是什么时候？

845
00:36:54.710 --> 00:36:57.890
And Stanley says, I have no idea because we're not friends.
斯坦利说，我根本不知道，因为我们不是朋友。

846
00:36:58.590 --> 00:37:05.550
You know, every single person wrote in about this to remind us that in season eight, episode
你知道的，几乎所有人都发信来提醒我们，在第八季第

847
00:37:05.550 --> 00:37:09.550
10, Jim says he got Stanley tickets to a comedy show for his birthday.
10集里，吉姆说他送过斯坦利喜剧秀的票作为他的生日礼物。

848
00:37:09.930 --> 00:37:11.870
So Jim knows Stanley's birthday.
所以吉姆知道斯坦利的生日。

849
00:37:12.110 --> 00:37:14.530
Or he's certainly celebrated it before.
或者他至少以前庆祝过。

850
00:37:14.750 --> 00:37:16.790
He must have a general idea of when it is.
他大概知道是什么时候。

851
00:37:16.790 --> 00:37:20.250
Well, Jim is going to offer to take them to lunch to discuss it further.
吉姆打算请他们吃午饭，以便进一步讨论。

852
00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:21.450
And now they're in.
然后他们就入局了。

853
00:37:21.790 --> 00:37:22.430
They're interested.
他们感兴趣了。

854
00:37:22.430 --> 00:37:23.050
They're up for a free lunch.
他们冲着免费午餐来的。

855
00:37:23.350 --> 00:37:23.490
Yeah.
没错。

856
00:37:24.050 --> 00:37:24.100
Yeah.
是啊。

857
00:37:24.850 --> 00:37:31.070
Outside, Dwight and Angela are walking down the sidewalk when Dwight shoves Angela into a van.
在外面，德怀特和安吉拉正走在人行道上，突然德怀特把安吉拉推进了一辆面包车。

858
00:37:31.570 --> 00:37:33.090
And we meet Trevor.
然后我们遇到了特雷弗。

859
00:37:34.070 --> 00:37:35.250
Call sheet tidbit.
拍摄通告单小花絮。

860
00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:39.570
This was the very first scene filmed on the very first day of filming.
这是开机第一天的第一场戏。

861
00:37:39.570 --> 00:37:42.870
So Chris, as the guest star, was first up.
所以克里斯作为客串明星，第一个上场。

862
00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:43.930
Wow.
哇。

863
00:37:44.190 --> 00:37:44.430
Right?
对吧？

864
00:37:44.670 --> 00:37:45.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

865
00:37:45.790 --> 00:37:47.670
Trevor says, is it safe to talk?
特雷弗问，说话安全吗？

866
00:37:47.870 --> 00:37:52.170
Dwight says, well, this documentary crew has been following our every move for the past nine
德怀特说，这摄制组过去九年里

867
00:37:52.170 --> 00:37:52.550
years.
一直对我们寸步不离。

868
00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:54.210
But I don't see him, so I think we're good.
但我没看到他们，所以我觉得我们安全了。

869
00:37:54.690 --> 00:37:56.730
Angela is going to ask Trevor, what are your credentials?
安吉拉要问特雷弗，你的资历是什么？

870
00:37:57.570 --> 00:38:00.430
And this line made me laugh so hard.
这句台词把我笑惨了。

871
00:38:01.350 --> 00:38:03.570
I broke when he said it the first time.
他第一次说的时候我就笑场了。

872
00:38:04.350 --> 00:38:09.810
With super seriousness, Trevor says, I started following people around to get exercise.
特雷弗极其严肃地说，我一开始跟着别人走是为了锻炼身体。

873
00:38:10.130 --> 00:38:12.010
Turns out, I'm damn good at it.
结果证明，我他妈太擅长这行了。

874
00:38:13.190 --> 00:38:14.450
I lost it.
我当时彻底笑崩了。

875
00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:17.740
Yes.
是的。

876
00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:20.780
Next question, they would like to know if he has a gun.
下一个问题，他们想知道他有没有枪。

877
00:38:21.180 --> 00:38:23.860
And he's like, do I have a gun?
然后他就反应说，我有枪吗？

878
00:38:24.060 --> 00:38:25.160
Check this out.
你看这个。

879
00:38:25.320 --> 00:38:26.660
He pulls out a receipt.
他掏出一张收据。

880
00:38:26.920 --> 00:38:28.460
He says, read the receipt.
他说，读一下收据。

881
00:38:29.060 --> 00:38:32.140
And Angela's like, what, you don't carry it with you?
然后安吉拉说，什么，你不随身带着吗？

882
00:38:32.240 --> 00:38:33.480
And he's like, it's expensive.
然后他说，这很贵。

883
00:38:33.480 --> 00:38:34.820
Someone could steal it.
别人会偷走的。

884
00:38:34.820 --> 00:38:38.520
And then Dwight says, you have no idea how many guns Trevor's had stolen.
接着德怀特说，你们根本不知道特雷弗被偷过多少把枪。

885
00:38:38.920 --> 00:38:41.440
And Trevor's like, yeah, now I keep it in a safe.
特雷弗就说，对啊，现在我把它锁在保险箱里。

886
00:38:41.440 --> 00:38:44.280
And then shows them the receipt of the safe.
然后向他们展示了保险箱的收据。

887
00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:47.060
This is something I have to share with you guys.
有个事我必须跟你们分享一下。

888
00:38:48.160 --> 00:38:51.860
This receipts bit went on for so long.
这个收据的包袱抖了太久了。

889
00:38:52.680 --> 00:38:54.240
Were there more receipts?
还有更多的收据吗？

890
00:38:54.420 --> 00:38:55.760
Chris started improvising.
克里斯开始即兴发挥了。

891
00:38:55.960 --> 00:38:58.280
You saw how many papers he's holding in his hands?
你们看到他手里拿了多少纸吗？

892
00:38:58.360 --> 00:38:58.660
Yes.
看到了。

893
00:38:58.880 --> 00:39:02.300
He just started improvising all the different things he has receipts for.
他开始即兴扯出各种他有收据的东西。

894
00:39:02.520 --> 00:39:03.040
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

895
00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:04.180
I was crying.
我都笑哭了。

896
00:39:04.180 --> 00:39:05.060
I was laughing.
我一直在笑。

897
00:39:05.340 --> 00:39:09.780
I was so hoping that I would find them in the bloopers or something.
我当时多么希望能的花絮里或者什么地方找到它们。

898
00:39:10.040 --> 00:39:11.520
I know they're out there somewhere.
我知道它们肯定在哪个角落里。

899
00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:13.820
But oh, my gosh.
但是，天哪。

900
00:39:14.360 --> 00:39:15.920
We did a lot of takes.
我们拍了好多条。

901
00:39:16.180 --> 00:39:19.120
And each time, he had more receipts for things.
而且每次他都有更多的收据。

902
00:39:19.720 --> 00:39:23.780
Well, you know, one of the things he shared with us was that when he runs into people who
嗯，你知道的，他跟我们分享的一件事是，当他遇到那些

903
00:39:23.780 --> 00:39:27.740
recognize him, they always say, check your receipts.
认出他的人时，他们总是说，去查查你的收据吧。

904
00:39:27.740 --> 00:39:28.260
Yes.
是的。

905
00:39:28.440 --> 00:39:29.840
And he's always like, wait, what?
而他总是那种反应，等等，什么？

906
00:39:29.940 --> 00:39:30.640
Oh, oh.
哦，哦。

907
00:39:30.920 --> 00:39:31.320
Yes.
是的。

908
00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:32.380
Check your receipts.
查查你的收据。

909
00:39:32.580 --> 00:39:33.640
It's his safe bandit.
那是他的安全大盗。

910
00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:34.980
Or don't throw garbage at me.
或者别朝我扔垃圾。

911
00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:35.520
Exactly.
没错。

912
00:39:36.020 --> 00:39:38.520
That's what perfect strangers say to him as he's walking through an airport.
当他走过机场时，完全不认识的陌生人就会对他说这些。

913
00:39:39.280 --> 00:39:43.380
Well, now we're going to go to the warehouse as Pam prepares to start painting.
好了，现在我们要去仓库，潘准备开始画画了。

914
00:39:43.940 --> 00:39:46.480
She's up on this big, what do you call that thing?
她站在那个大大的，那个叫什么来着？

915
00:39:46.480 --> 00:39:48.080
Like a scaffolding thing.
就像那种脚手架一样的东西。

916
00:39:48.080 --> 00:39:48.460
Yeah.
对。

917
00:39:48.820 --> 00:39:49.740
It's like a scaffold thing.
就像个脚手架。

918
00:39:49.840 --> 00:39:50.020
Yeah.
对。

919
00:39:50.360 --> 00:39:52.920
And she's put a grid up in pencil.
她用铅笔画好了网格。

920
00:39:53.240 --> 00:39:54.680
And she's looking at her sketches.
她正在看她的草图。

921
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:56.020
She's getting prepared.
她正在做准备。

922
00:39:56.820 --> 00:39:58.380
She's going to start this.
她要开始这个了。

923
00:39:58.780 --> 00:39:58.940
Yeah.
对。

924
00:39:59.040 --> 00:39:59.760
She says, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

925
00:39:59.760 --> 00:40:01.920
If I mess up, I can just cover it with a shrub.
如果我搞砸了，我可以用一丛灌木把它盖住。

926
00:40:02.220 --> 00:40:02.580
Yeah.
对。

927
00:40:02.580 --> 00:40:08.480
This talking head of Pam's was actually longer by one sentence and it cracked me up.
潘的这个采访镜头实际上多了一句话，把我逗乐了。

928
00:40:08.580 --> 00:40:10.080
Here's how it read in the shooting draft.
拍摄初稿里的内容是这样的。

929
00:40:10.280 --> 00:40:13.480
I guess if I make a mistake, I can just cover it up with a shrub or something.
我想如果我犯了错误，我可以用灌木丛或其他什么东西把它盖住。

930
00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:16.700
But I always think less of paintings that are full of shrubs.
但我总是看不起那些到处都是灌木丛的画作。

931
00:40:16.840 --> 00:40:19.600
I'm only allowing myself one shrub.
我只允许自己画一丛灌木。

932
00:40:19.800 --> 00:40:22.960
And then here's the line that she would have said.
然后是她本该说的那句台词。

933
00:40:23.640 --> 00:40:25.660
Two shrubs and a guy with a big umbrella.
两丛灌木和一个撑着大伞的家伙。

934
00:40:25.960 --> 00:40:26.300
Tops.
不能再多了。

935
00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:27.460
Nice.
