来自北卡罗来纳州谢尔比的

1260
00:52:58.810 --> 00:53:00.730
from Shelby, North Carolina said,
艾莉森·M 说，

1261
00:53:08.930 --> 00:53:10.270
And Jessica N.
而来自纽约州罗切斯特的

1262
00:53:10.410 --> 00:53:11.970
from Rochester, New York said,
杰西卡·N 说，

1263
00:53:12.470 --> 00:53:17.570
Do you know if there were any structures that were possibly glued together for some of the scenes?
你知道在某些场景中是不是有什么结构可能是粘在一起的吗？

1264
00:53:17.910 --> 00:53:22.730
Or were they all legit card structures that just didn't make it through some of the takes?
还是说它们全都是真正的纸牌结构，只是在某些镜头里没能撑过去？

1265
00:53:22.910 --> 00:53:24.330
They had to have been glued together.
它们肯定是被粘在一起的。

1266
00:53:24.670 --> 00:53:25.350
They were.
确实是。

1267
00:53:25.570 --> 00:53:25.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1268
00:53:25.730 --> 00:53:28.570
This was such an elaborate prop, actually.
其实这是一个非常精致的道具。

1269
00:53:29.010 --> 00:53:30.770
Kudos again to Phil Shea.
再次向菲尔·希a致敬。

1270
00:53:31.370 --> 00:53:37.610
Steve Burgess said that we had about six different versions of the tower in various stages.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说我们大约有六个不同阶段的塔的版本。

1271
00:53:38.070 --> 00:53:43.890
And then when I was talking with Brent, he reminded me that they built it in layers.
然后我和布伦特聊天时，他提醒我它们是分层建造的。

1272
00:53:44.590 --> 00:53:47.930
So there would be like the bottom layer that was all glued together.
所以会有一个全都是粘在一起的底层。

1273
00:53:48.090 --> 00:53:51.030
And then we could add like another layer that was all glued together.
然后我们可以加上另一个全都是粘在一起的层。

1274
00:53:51.030 --> 00:53:56.830
I do remember that, that they would carry them in on almost like this, I don't know, like a tray,
我确实记得这一点，他们会几乎像用这个一样把它们端进来，我不知道，就像一个托盘，

1275
00:53:57.030 --> 00:54:00.430
like a big flat piece of plywood they would carry in a layer at a time.
就像一块大而平的合板，他们每次搬进来一层。

1276
00:54:00.690 --> 00:54:01.110
Yes.
是的。

1277
00:54:01.350 --> 00:54:01.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1278
00:54:01.570 --> 00:54:05.550
And Steve Burgess actually sent me a bunch of pictures of us posing around the towers.
而且史蒂夫·伯吉斯实际上给我发了一堆我们围着塔摆姿势的照片。

1279
00:54:05.550 --> 00:54:07.630
So you can put those in stories, Angela.
所以你可以把它们发到动态里，安吉拉。

1280
00:54:07.950 --> 00:54:14.270
But Brent said there was one exception, you know, the scene when Kevin has to knock the tower down.
但布伦特说有一个例外，你知道的，就是凯文不得不把塔撞倒的那个场景。

1281
00:54:14.530 --> 00:54:14.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1282
00:54:14.850 --> 00:54:20.650
That was a real tower of cards, and it took a very long time to build.
那是一座真正的纸牌屋，搭起来花了很长时间。

1283
00:54:20.910 --> 00:54:23.090
We filmed that in two parts.
我们分两部分拍摄了那个场景。

1284
00:54:23.370 --> 00:54:29.750
Brent said we did six takes of the scene right up until the moment when Kevin knocks the tower down.
布伦特说，对于凯文把塔撞倒之前的那一刻，我们拍了六条。

1285
00:54:30.270 --> 00:54:33.590
Then we did one take of him knocking the tower down.
然后我们拍了一条他把塔撞倒的镜头。

1286
00:54:33.770 --> 00:54:40.470
And then we did six takes of the second half of the scene when the cards were all splayed out.
接着我们拍了六条场景后半部分纸牌散落一地的镜头。

1287
00:54:40.570 --> 00:54:40.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1288
00:54:40.750 --> 00:54:48.430
So he only had to knock the tower down once, but this was really important because you didn't know where the cards were going to go when they fell.
所以他只需要把塔撞倒一次，但这真的很重要，因为你不知道它们倒下时纸牌会飞到哪里去。

1289
00:54:48.570 --> 00:54:53.750
So it was kind of like an impossible continuity thing to try to recreate the cards falling.
所以这有点像一个不可能完成的连戏任务，去试图重现纸牌倒下的样子。

1290
00:54:53.990 --> 00:55:00.010
So that's why once they fell, we just left them where they were, and we did the end of the scene six times.
这就是为什么一旦它们倒了，我们就让它们原封不动，然后把场景的结尾拍了六遍。

1291
00:55:00.510 --> 00:55:07.010
Shout out to Brian Baumgartner because this is yet another time where he has to get it basically in one take.
向布莱因·鲍姆加特纳致敬，因为这又是他基本上必须一条过的时候。

1292
00:55:07.170 --> 00:55:07.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1293
00:55:07.350 --> 00:55:09.190
He had to spill that whole pot of chili.
他必须把整锅辣椒都洒了。

1294
00:55:09.470 --> 00:55:09.670
Yep.
没错。

1295
00:55:09.670 --> 00:55:11.370
And then one little area.
然后还有一个小区域。

1296
00:55:11.630 --> 00:55:11.810
Yep.
没错。

1297
00:55:11.950 --> 00:55:15.850
And then now he has to knock down this tower of cards and not mess it up.
而现在他不得不推倒这座纸牌屋还不能搞砸。

1298
00:55:16.010 --> 00:55:16.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1299
00:55:16.450 --> 00:55:20.610
You know, like what if he hit the middle by accident or, you know.
你知道的，比如万一他不小心打中了中间，或者什么的。

1300
00:55:20.830 --> 00:55:21.230
Yes.
是的。

1301
00:55:21.310 --> 00:55:28.730
If it hadn't fallen correctly, we would have had to wait for them to build the whole thing again in order to get the fall right.
如果它没能顺利倒塌，我们就得等他们把整个建筑重新搭好，才能拍好倒塌的镜头。

1302
00:55:28.930 --> 00:55:29.110
Yeah.
对。

1303
00:55:29.370 --> 00:55:32.050
And then, of course, the subsequent takes afterwards.
然后，当然还有接下来的后续镜头。

1304
00:55:32.370 --> 00:55:33.090
Way to go, Brian.
干得好，布莱恩。

1305
00:55:33.270 --> 00:55:34.090
Way to go, Brian.
干得好，布莱恩。

1306
00:55:34.090 --> 00:55:35.990
I would like to share.
我想分享一下。

1307
00:55:35.990 --> 00:55:39.310
I would like to hear that someone is really noticing how sweet Pete is.
我想听听有人真正注意到皮特有多贴心。

1308
00:55:39.850 --> 00:55:40.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1309
00:55:40.230 --> 00:55:40.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1310
00:55:41.090 --> 00:55:45.110
When Kevin knocks it all down and everyone's upset at him, Pete says, you know what?
当凯文把一切都推倒，所有人都生他的气时，皮特说，你知道吗？

1311
00:55:45.190 --> 00:55:46.310
He made a mistake.
他只是犯了个错。

1312
00:55:46.450 --> 00:55:48.610
And isn't that what that whole tower is about anyway?
而且这不也正是整座纸牌塔的意义所在吗？

1313
00:55:49.010 --> 00:55:52.770
And he gives Kevin a fist bump and he says, let's get back to work.
然后他跟凯文碰了拳，并说，我们回去工作吧。

1314
00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:54.650
Aaron is all smiles.
亚伦满脸笑容。

1315
00:55:54.650 --> 00:55:59.170
And there was a deleted talking head where Aaron talks about Pete.
还有一个被删掉的单人访谈镜头，亚伦在里面谈到了皮特。

1316
00:55:59.230 --> 00:56:00.450
And I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

1317
00:56:01.030 --> 00:56:03.070
Pete really sticks up for the underdog.
皮特真的很维护弱势群体。

1318
00:56:03.490 --> 00:56:06.650
And in my book, that's the best dog to stick up for.
在我看来，那才是最应该去维护的“弱者”。

1319
00:56:06.850 --> 00:56:11.030
The little dog that's underneath all the other dogs, way at the bottom.
就是被压在所有其他狗下面、最底层的那个小狗。

1320
00:56:12.090 --> 00:56:12.710
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

1321
00:56:13.130 --> 00:56:14.090
Good guy, this Pete.
真是个好人，这个皮特。

1322
00:56:14.290 --> 00:56:15.110
I like this guy.
我喜欢这家伙。

1323
00:56:15.830 --> 00:56:16.630
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1324
00:56:16.630 --> 00:56:18.590
I love the definition of underdog.
我太喜欢他对“underdog”（弱者/底层）的解释了。

1325
00:56:18.710 --> 00:56:19.210
I know.
就是说啊。

1326
00:56:19.620 --> 00:56:24.350
I love the idea that there's a pile of dogs and there's a little tiny one underneath all
我喜欢那种脑补画面：有一堆狗，然后有一只超级小的小狗被压在它们

1327
00:56:24.350 --> 00:56:24.870
of them.
所有狗的底下。

1328
00:56:25.190 --> 00:56:26.090
Got to get him out of there.
得赶紧把它从里面救出来。

1329
00:56:26.410 --> 00:56:32.190
You know, another thing that Pete says is, come on, who in here hasn't gotten a complaint
你知道的，皮特说的另一句话是，拜托，这里面谁没收到过投诉

1330
00:56:32.190 --> 00:56:33.250
or made a mistake?
或者犯过错呢？

1331
00:56:34.250 --> 00:56:36.270
And Pam raises her hand.
然后潘举起了手。

1332
00:56:36.270 --> 00:56:38.770
She's never had a complaint against her.
她从来没有被人投诉过。

1333
00:56:38.950 --> 00:56:39.930
Not ever?
从来没有？

1334
00:56:39.930 --> 00:56:45.290
With all the pranks she's done with Jim over the years, Dwight hasn't filed a complaint?
这些年来她和吉姆搞了那么多恶作剧，德怀特居然没投诉过？

1335
00:56:45.290 --> 00:56:47.450
Well, I think it's customer complaint, right?
哦，我想是指客户投诉吧？

1336
00:56:47.450 --> 00:56:48.570
Oh, yes, yes, yes.
哦，对，对，对。

1337
00:56:48.570 --> 00:56:48.870
Yes.
是的。

1338
00:56:48.870 --> 00:56:49.910
Okay, okay, yes.
好吧，好吧，是的。

1339
00:56:49.910 --> 00:56:52.490
I'm sure there's been files of Dwight complaints.
我敢肯定关于德怀特的投诉档案有一大堆。

1340
00:56:52.630 --> 00:56:53.510
Oh, yeah, you're right.
哦，对，你说的对。

1341
00:56:54.010 --> 00:56:58.890
So now the tower has been rebuilt and it is almost up to the ceiling.
所以现在纸牌塔已经重建好了，而且快要碰到天花板了。

1342
00:56:59.210 --> 00:56:59.390
Yeah.
对。

1343
00:56:59.610 --> 00:57:00.850
And they've run out of cards.
而且他们的纸牌用完了。

1344
00:57:01.090 --> 00:57:02.730
There's no more complaints.
没有更多的投诉信了。

1345
00:57:03.130 --> 00:57:06.370
They just need one more complaint to make it to the ceiling.
他们只需要再来一张投诉信就能搭到天花板了。

1346
00:57:06.850 --> 00:57:09.550
So Pam is going to volunteer to get a complaint.
所以潘打算主动去弄一张投诉信来。

1347
00:57:10.110 --> 00:57:11.430
Meredith doesn't buy it.
梅雷迪思根本不信。

1348
00:57:11.610 --> 00:57:12.690
She says, you know what, Pam?
她说，你知道吗，潘？

1349
00:57:12.990 --> 00:57:14.590
She wouldn't fart on a butterfly.
她连对蝴蝶放个屁都舍不得。

1350
00:57:14.590 --> 00:57:20.650
And then, Jenna, the way you as Pam said the line, I can't even relate to that impulse.
然后，珍娜，你作为潘说那句台词的方式——我甚至无法理解那种冲动。

1351
00:57:21.150 --> 00:57:23.410
It was so funny the way you said it.
你刚才说话的语气太搞笑了。

1352
00:57:23.770 --> 00:57:29.350
Well, one thing I remember from this particular scene was that the first time we had what was
嗯，我记得这个特定场景的一点是，我们第一次搭那座

1353
00:57:29.350 --> 00:57:32.150
going to be the tallest tower, Greg said it wasn't tall enough.
将要成为最高的塔时，格雷格说还不够高。

1354
00:57:32.890 --> 00:57:33.110
What?
什么？

1355
00:57:33.110 --> 00:57:33.670
Yeah.
对。

1356
00:57:33.890 --> 00:57:37.970
He said, I want the top card to touch the ceiling.
他说，我想要最上面的牌碰到天花板。

1357
00:57:38.410 --> 00:57:40.610
He's like, that's when they know they've done it.
他觉得，只有那样他们才知道自己成功了。

1358
00:57:40.770 --> 00:57:42.590
I have to say, I agree with that.
我得说，我赞同这一点。

1359
00:57:42.810 --> 00:57:46.250
That feels like, okay, we've literally reached the ceiling.
那感觉就像是，好吧，我们真的触及天花板了。

1360
00:57:46.450 --> 00:57:46.710
Yes.
没错。

1361
00:57:47.170 --> 00:57:52.290
Well, Pam is definitely part of the camaraderie now because everyone is chanting, Pam, Pam, Pam, Pam.
好吧，帕姆现在绝对融入集体了，因为大家都在齐声喊：帕姆，帕姆，帕姆，帕姆。

1362
00:57:52.650 --> 00:57:55.690
Except maybe someone in the warehouse would be chanting, Pat, Pat, Pat.
不过仓库里可能有人会喊：帕特，帕特，帕特。

1363
00:57:55.690 --> 00:57:55.930
That's true.
确实。

1364
00:57:56.870 --> 00:57:57.770
Very true.
太对了。

1365
00:57:58.450 --> 00:58:04.390
Well, back at Jim's lunch, Phyllis is, what would you call it?
好了，回到吉姆的午餐，菲利斯这是在，你该怎么形容呢？

1366
00:58:04.510 --> 00:58:06.930
She's looking at her hands.
她正看着自己的双手。

1367
00:58:07.150 --> 00:58:09.630
She's seeing the passage of time.
她看到了岁月的流逝。

1368
00:58:09.850 --> 00:58:12.510
I thought Phyllis was so brilliant in this scene.
我觉得菲利斯在这场戏里演得太精彩了。

1369
00:58:12.850 --> 00:58:14.210
She says, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1370
00:58:14.210 --> 00:58:19.010
I don't know where the years went because sometimes when I look at my hands, I don't even recognize
我不知道这些年都去哪儿了，因为有时当我看着自己的双手，我甚至都认不出来

1371
00:58:19.010 --> 00:58:19.430
them.
它们了。

1372
00:58:20.030 --> 00:58:22.110
And she goes, whose hands are these?
然后她说，这是谁的手啊？

1373
00:58:22.110 --> 00:58:27.010
And then she kind of folds them into her body and she's like, they're not my hands.
接着她把手收到身体两侧，一副这根本不是我的手的样子。

1374
00:58:27.170 --> 00:58:27.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1375
00:58:28.370 --> 00:58:31.650
And Jim's like, oh, gosh, I'm not getting anywhere.
吉姆则是一脸，天哪，我完全说不通啊。

1376
00:58:31.830 --> 00:58:33.010
Phyllis is so drunk.
菲利斯喝得太醉了。

1377
00:58:33.330 --> 00:58:35.350
You know what this scene made me think of?
你知道这个场景让我想起了什么吗？

1378
00:58:35.550 --> 00:58:39.210
I remember, I think I must have been in like my mid-40s.
我记得，我当时大概是在四十岁左右吧。

1379
00:58:39.630 --> 00:58:47.270
One morning, I looked down at my hands and I got like immediately emotional because my hands
有一天早上，我低头看着自己的双手，瞬间就有点情绪失控了，因为我的手

1380
00:58:47.270 --> 00:58:49.330
looked just like my mother's hands.
看起来简直和我母亲的手一模一样。

1381
00:58:49.470 --> 00:58:49.930
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1382
00:58:49.930 --> 00:58:56.530
And I thought one day she's not going to be here anymore, but she's always going to be
我想象着总有一天她会不在了，但她会永远留

1383
00:58:56.530 --> 00:58:57.410
in my hands.
在我的手上。

1384
00:58:57.650 --> 00:58:57.850
Yeah.
对。

1385
00:58:57.990 --> 00:58:58.990
I'm going to see her.
我总能见到她。

1386
00:58:59.150 --> 00:59:02.130
And I do see her when I look at my hands, even now.
现在每当我看着自己的手，也确实能看到她。

1387
00:59:02.470 --> 00:59:03.870
It's so special to me.
这对我来说太特别了。

1388
00:59:04.210 --> 00:59:04.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1389
00:59:04.790 --> 00:59:05.190
Yeah.
对。

1390
00:59:05.350 --> 00:59:10.450
I started looking more and more like my mother as I get older, even in my face and everything
随着年龄增长，我越来越像我母亲了，甚至连脸型和其它方面

1391
00:59:10.450 --> 00:59:11.030
like that.
都一样。

1392
00:59:11.190 --> 00:59:13.590
Growing up, I thought I didn't really look like either of my parents.
从小到大，我还以为自己长得一点都不像父母呢。

1393
00:59:13.590 --> 00:59:18.770
So when Phyllis was giving this big speech about whose hands are these, I like remember
所以当菲利斯发表那番关于这是谁的手的长篇大论时，我想起

1394
00:59:18.770 --> 00:59:23.350
the day I felt like I went from having my hands to, oh, my gosh, I have my mother's
了我觉得自己从拥有自己的手，变成天哪，我拥有了母亲的

1395
00:59:23.350 --> 00:59:23.750
hands.
手的那一天。

1396
00:59:24.210 --> 00:59:24.310
Yeah.
对。

1397
00:59:24.610 --> 00:59:24.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1398
00:59:25.250 --> 00:59:26.350
No, I get that too.
不，我也有同感。

1399
00:59:26.670 --> 00:59:30.510
My dad's index fingers turned in and so do mine.
我爸爸的食指是往里扣的，我的也是。

1400
00:59:31.070 --> 00:59:31.930
Yours do.
你的也是。

1401
00:59:32.350 --> 00:59:32.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1402
00:59:32.630 --> 00:59:34.530
I never noticed that about you.
我以前从没注意到你这一点。

1403
00:59:34.710 --> 00:59:35.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1404
00:59:35.490 --> 00:59:35.970
And he's—
而且他——

1405
00:59:35.970 --> 00:59:36.610
I see it.
我懂。

1406
00:59:37.110 --> 00:59:42.390
He's no longer here, but I think about that when I look at my hands.
他已经不在了，但我看着自己的双手时就会想起那件事。

1407
00:59:43.630 --> 00:59:44.110
Sorry.
抱歉。

1408
00:59:44.310 --> 00:59:44.890
That was okay.
刚刚挺好的。

1409
00:59:46.590 --> 00:59:47.490
This is like—
这就像是——

1410
00:59:47.490 --> 00:59:48.130
Sorry, everyone.
大家抱歉。

1411
00:59:48.130 --> 00:59:50.050
