Like, this guy just frisked you.
比如，这个人刚刚才对你进行了搜身。

1553
01:07:03.070 --> 01:07:03.430
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

1554
01:07:03.430 --> 01:07:04.530
And then was like, by the way.
然后就像是，顺便说一句。

1555
01:07:05.110 --> 01:07:08.390
Yes, and also because you've been frisked, right?
对，而且也是因为你刚被搜身过，对吧？

1556
01:07:08.550 --> 01:07:08.690
Yeah.
对。

1557
01:07:08.690 --> 01:07:11.730
And you think you have anonymity while the frisking is happening.
而且你以为在搜身的过程中你是匿名的。

1558
01:07:11.910 --> 01:07:12.130
Yes.
是的。

1559
01:07:12.250 --> 01:07:15.650
And then as you're leaving the frisk, you realize, oh.
然后当你搜身结束离开时，你意识到，哦。

1560
01:07:16.090 --> 01:07:16.510
Yes.
是的。

1561
01:07:16.730 --> 01:07:17.130
Okay.
好吧。

1562
01:07:17.590 --> 01:07:19.070
That's just one example.
这只是其中一个例子。

1563
01:07:19.090 --> 01:07:19.770
Just one day.
仅仅一天。

1564
01:07:19.970 --> 01:07:20.590
Of hundreds.
数以百计中的一天。

1565
01:07:20.590 --> 01:07:24.290
There are truly so many examples, just like Chris's.
真的有太多的例子了，就像克里斯的那样。

1566
01:07:24.650 --> 01:07:25.690
Yes, there are.
是的，确实有。

1567
01:07:25.790 --> 01:07:26.470
We have so many.
我们有超级多。

1568
01:07:26.670 --> 01:07:30.190
But, you know, obviously, we're so appreciative that people love the show.
但是，你知道，显然，我们非常感激大家喜欢这个节目。

1569
01:07:30.330 --> 01:07:32.050
But sometimes the timing.
但有时候这个时机。

1570
01:07:32.450 --> 01:07:34.130
Sometimes the timing could be better.
有时候时机可以更好一点。

1571
01:07:34.530 --> 01:07:37.490
Maybe mention it before the frisk.
也许在搜身之前提出来。

1572
01:07:37.630 --> 01:07:39.490
I think you want it after the frisk.
我觉得你更希望在搜身之后吧。

1573
01:07:39.810 --> 01:07:42.990
I do think if you're going to say something, do it after a frisk.
我确实觉得如果要说什么的话，要在搜身之后说。

1574
01:07:43.130 --> 01:07:43.370
After the.
在那个。

1575
01:07:43.550 --> 01:07:44.430
I think.
我觉得。

1576
01:07:44.630 --> 01:07:44.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1577
01:07:45.150 --> 01:07:45.430
Okay.
好的。

1578
01:07:45.690 --> 01:07:45.950
Right?
对吧？

1579
01:07:46.350 --> 01:07:47.330
Yeah, maybe so.
对，也许吧。

1580
01:07:47.470 --> 01:07:48.250
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

1581
01:07:48.970 --> 01:07:51.110
Well, now Dwight and Oscar are in the warehouse.
好了，现在德怀特和奥斯卡在仓库里。

1582
01:07:51.670 --> 01:07:56.750
And Dwight tells him what was going on, that they were going to break his kneecaps.
德怀特告诉了他刚才发生了什么，他们打算打断他的膝盖骨。

1583
01:07:57.290 --> 01:08:00.650
And he says, of all the gorgeous men in the Scranton-Wilkes-Barre area,
然后他说，在斯克兰顿-威尔克斯-巴里地区所有的美男子中，

1584
01:08:00.650 --> 01:08:03.150
why did you have to choose the father of Angela's child?
为什么你偏偏要选安吉拉孩子的父亲？

1585
01:08:03.990 --> 01:08:04.870
Come on.
拜托。

1586
01:08:05.310 --> 01:08:07.570
Dwight is still trying to just get Oscar out of there.
德怀特仍然只是想把奥斯卡弄走。

1587
01:08:07.690 --> 01:08:10.190
He rushes them out of the warehouse into the alleyway.
他催促他们离开仓库走到小巷里。

1588
01:08:10.390 --> 01:08:11.230
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1589
01:08:11.390 --> 01:08:12.450
Trevor is right there.
特雷弗就在那里。

1590
01:08:12.530 --> 01:08:16.010
And he is determined for once to follow through with something.
他难得下定决心要贯彻到底完成一件事。

1591
01:08:16.450 --> 01:08:21.610
So the three of them end up kind of scuffling, struggling over this pipe.
所以他们三个人最终扭打在了一起，为了这根管子争夺不休。

1592
01:08:21.890 --> 01:08:23.750
Dwight and Oscar are trying to get it away from Trevor.
德怀特和奥斯卡试图从特雷弗手中夺走它。

1593
01:08:23.930 --> 01:08:26.430
Trevor's trying to complete the job for which he was hired.
特雷弗正试图完成他受雇要做的工作。

1594
01:08:27.210 --> 01:08:28.090
Oscar prevails.
奥斯卡占了上风。

1595
01:08:28.090 --> 01:08:29.110
He gets the pipe.
他拿到了管子。

1596
01:08:29.490 --> 01:08:33.950
I asked Steve Burgess if we had a fight coordinator or a stunt coordinator for this fight.
我问史蒂夫·伯吉斯我们为这场打斗有没有请打斗统筹或特技统筹。

1597
01:08:33.990 --> 01:08:34.950
And he said no.
他说没有。

1598
01:08:35.270 --> 01:08:35.530
No.
没有。

1599
01:08:35.930 --> 01:08:39.150
They just let the three of them sort it out.
他们就任由他们三个人自己解决。

1600
01:08:39.310 --> 01:08:39.590
Yeah.
对。

1601
01:08:40.210 --> 01:08:42.050
Well, I asked Chris about this scene.
嗯，我问过克里斯关于这场戏的事。

1602
01:08:42.070 --> 01:08:43.690
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

1603
01:08:43.690 --> 01:08:48.930
As far as the fight scene, I remember the day moving pretty quickly.
就打斗戏而言，我记得那天进度挺快的。

1604
01:08:49.210 --> 01:08:54.510
I remember being pretty intimidated, even though obviously everyone on set was so nice.
我记得当时挺紧张的，尽管片场显然每个人都非常友好。

1605
01:08:54.830 --> 01:08:56.930
But I felt like things could get wild.
但我总觉得事情可能会失控。

1606
01:08:57.170 --> 01:08:58.390
But it all went well.
不过一切都很顺利。

1607
01:08:58.390 --> 01:09:03.310
I remember being slightly different each time because we were kind of really wrestling around.
我记得每次感觉都有点不同，因为我们真的是在互相扭打。

1608
01:09:03.790 --> 01:09:06.310
I think I like that.
我想我挺喜欢那样的。

1609
01:09:06.550 --> 01:09:11.110
I like the idea of if we're going to do something physical and we're not supposed to be trained fighters,
我喜欢这种想法，如果我们要做一些肢体冲突的戏，而且我们又不是受过训练的格斗家，

1610
01:09:11.170 --> 01:09:14.790
like we might as well go for it and see where our bodies go because that'll be natural.
那我们就索性放手去干，看看我们的身体会怎么做，因为那样会很自然。

1611
01:09:14.890 --> 01:09:19.710
I also got the sense that Rain was probably into that.
我也觉得雷恩大概也很喜欢那样。

1612
01:09:20.090 --> 01:09:24.470
Oscar, I think, was probably the one who was the most reserved about, wait, what's exactly going to happen?
我想奥斯卡可能才是那个最有所保留的人，心想，等等，到底会发生什么？

1613
01:09:24.470 --> 01:09:33.250
And I think Rain and I have remained, you know, not super tight, but we touch base every couple of years just to see how the other one's doing and cross paths.
而且我觉得我和雷恩一直以来，你知道的，虽然算不上超级铁，但每隔几年都会联系一下，看看对方过得怎么样，偶尔也会碰面。

1614
01:09:33.450 --> 01:09:41.190
And I do get the sense he and I both probably have a similar sense of, well, if we're doing some scene that's supposed to be some crazy unplanned wrestling match,
而且我确实觉得我和他可能都有这样一种共识，那就是，如果我们拍一场本来应该是那种疯狂的、毫无计划的扭打戏，

1615
01:09:41.330 --> 01:09:44.470
the easiest way to do it is just let's start wrestling.
最简单的办法就是直接开始扭打。

1616
01:09:44.890 --> 01:09:46.030
So that was pretty fun.
所以那挺有意思的。

1617
01:09:47.170 --> 01:09:51.030
Chris, I would confirm that that would be Rain's take on that.
克里斯，我可以证实那确实是雷恩对这件事的看法。

1618
01:09:51.190 --> 01:09:51.970
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

1619
01:09:52.210 --> 01:09:52.470
Yes.
是的。

1620
01:09:52.470 --> 01:09:59.830
I also asked Chris if any of his improvs made it into the episode because, you know, he was so funny.
我还问了克里斯他的即兴发挥有没有被用到这集里，因为，你知道的，他太搞笑了。

1621
01:10:00.050 --> 01:10:02.990
And yes, we got everything scripted and it was so well written.
是的，剧本里的内容我们都拍了，而且写得太棒了。

1622
01:10:03.310 --> 01:10:06.530
But there were these great moments of improvisation from him.
但其中也有他非常精彩的即兴发挥时刻。

1623
01:10:06.650 --> 01:10:07.810
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

1624
01:10:08.710 --> 01:10:12.610
I do remember improvising a line in the fight with Oscar.
我确实记得在与奥斯卡的打斗中即兴发挥了一句台词。

1625
01:10:13.350 --> 01:10:15.590
If I remember right, I run away.
如果我没记错的话，我跑开了。

1626
01:10:15.590 --> 01:10:22.030
And while I run away, I'm shouting something along the lines of I have masculinity issues.
而且在我逃跑的时候，我大喊着类似于“我有男性气概问题”之类的话。

1627
01:10:22.470 --> 01:10:24.450
And that line was improvised.
那句台词是即兴发挥的。

1628
01:10:24.650 --> 01:10:27.590
I remember being psyched that they used that.
我记得他们用了那句台词时我感到非常兴奋。

1629
01:10:28.630 --> 01:10:30.010
Oh, that is so fun.
哦，那太有趣了。

1630
01:10:30.170 --> 01:10:34.130
Chris also had talked about just how amazing the writing was.
克里斯还谈到了剧本写得是多么惊艳。

1631
01:10:34.530 --> 01:10:36.690
And he said, like,
他说，比如，

1632
01:10:36.930 --> 01:10:47.570
one of the reasons he was so tickled to get an improv line in was because he knew it was going to have to really be good in order to make it because all the scripted stuff was so good.
他之所以能有一句即兴台词被采用感到那么高兴，原因之一就是他知道台词必须真的非常好才能被选上，因为所有写好的台词都太棒了。

1633
01:10:47.570 --> 01:10:47.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1634
01:10:48.390 --> 01:10:51.210
Well, we got a fan question about this scene from Carly P.
好吧，我们收到了一条关于这场戏的粉丝提问，来自伊利诺伊州凯撒市的卡莉·P。

1635
01:10:51.430 --> 01:10:52.270
in Cesar, Illinois.
伊利诺伊州凯撒市。

1636
01:10:53.010 --> 01:11:02.650
And Carly said this, when Dwight, Oscar, and Trevor are fighting over the pipe, there are people passing by in the background on the street.
卡莉是这么说的，当德怀特、奥斯卡和特雷弗在抢夺一根管子时，背景的街道上有路人经过。

1637
01:11:03.010 --> 01:11:08.450
Were these just actual passerbys or were they staged to walk past at this point?
这些只是真正的路人，还是他们被安排在这个时候走过去的？

1638
01:11:08.630 --> 01:11:13.090
Because they do not look concerned about three grown men rolling on the ground fighting over a lead pipe.
因为他们看起来对三个成年人在地上滚来滚去抢一根铅管一点也不担心。

1639
01:11:14.210 --> 01:11:16.830
Carly, I did not notice this at firSt.
卡莉，我一开始没有注意到这一点。

1640
01:11:16.830 --> 01:11:20.690
I went back and I rewatched the scene and I see this couple walk by.
我回去重新看了这场戏，然后我看到了这对夫妇走过。

1641
01:11:21.310 --> 01:11:24.370
I think they're just two people who walked down the street.
我想他们只是两个顺便走过这条街的人。

1642
01:11:24.670 --> 01:11:26.850
Carly, I went back and looked as well.
卡莉，我也回去看过了。

1643
01:11:27.090 --> 01:11:29.990
They are 100% just two people walking down the street.
他们百分之百只是两个走在街上的人。

1644
01:11:30.830 --> 01:11:38.390
I think the other thing that's going on here is that we had been filming this show for nine years at this location.
我觉得这里还有另一个情况，那就是我们在同一个地点拍摄这部剧已经九年了。

1645
01:11:38.470 --> 01:11:41.350
And there were other businesses right next to us.
而且我们旁边还有其他的商铺。

1646
01:11:41.470 --> 01:11:44.630
And at this point, they just knew, oh, it's that TV show.
到了这个时候，他们已经知道了，哦，那是那个电视剧剧组。

1647
01:11:44.630 --> 01:11:51.670
So I think when they saw three men, like, tussling, they were like, oh, they're doing, they're filming something.
所以我觉得当他们看到三个男人在，呃，扭打时，他们会想，哦，他们在演，他们在拍什么东西。

1648
01:11:51.670 --> 01:11:52.330
I don't know.
我不知道。

1649
01:11:52.470 --> 01:11:54.010
That is exactly what I thought as well.
这正是我所想的。

1650
01:11:54.290 --> 01:11:58.370
Well, now it's Pam's turn to try to get a complaint, right?
好了，现在轮到帕姆去试着投诉了，对吧？

1651
01:11:58.610 --> 01:11:58.790
Yep.
没错。

1652
01:11:59.170 --> 01:12:02.570
Erin and Nellie and Creed are really encouraging her to fail.
艾琳、内莉和克里德真的在怂恿她失败。

1653
01:12:02.570 --> 01:12:05.150
Well, they say you got to think like a scumbag.
嗯，他们说你得像个人渣一样思考。

1654
01:12:05.590 --> 01:12:07.730
Creed shows her, but then just looks off into space.
克里德示范了一下，然后就双眼无神地发呆了。

1655
01:12:07.870 --> 01:12:08.970
It's like this.
就像这样。

1656
01:12:09.470 --> 01:12:15.610
Pam calls a client and does your mama's so fat joke and hangs up on them.
帕姆给客户打电话，讲了一个你妈真胖的笑话然后就挂了。

1657
01:12:16.690 --> 01:12:20.030
Erin's phone immediately rings and she takes the message.
艾琳的电话立刻响了，她接下了留言。

1658
01:12:20.150 --> 01:12:20.650
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1659
01:12:20.970 --> 01:12:22.190
They lost a client.
他们失去了一个客户。

1660
01:12:22.330 --> 01:12:22.710
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

1661
01:12:22.710 --> 01:12:23.730
Everyone's like, woo-hoo!
大家都觉得，呜呼！

1662
01:12:23.910 --> 01:12:25.110
But then they're like, oh, wait, crap.
但接着他们又觉得，噢，等等，糟糕。

1663
01:12:25.250 --> 01:12:26.150
We lost a client.
我们失去了一个客户。

1664
01:12:26.150 --> 01:12:27.830
That was, we just wanted a complaint.
那是，我们只是想要个投诉。

1665
01:12:28.230 --> 01:12:28.430
A complaint.
一个投诉。

1666
01:12:29.250 --> 01:12:31.370
Jenna, you're so good in this scene.
珍娜，你在这场戏里演得太好了。

1667
01:12:31.630 --> 01:12:33.590
I thought you just were great.
我觉得你真是太棒了。

1668
01:12:33.730 --> 01:12:34.590
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1669
01:12:34.730 --> 01:12:35.690
Brent thought so too.
布伦特也这么觉得。

1670
01:12:35.910 --> 01:12:36.870
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他的评价。

1671
01:12:37.570 --> 01:12:45.830
The Tower of Complaints subplot is one of those big group stories that becomes so useful to the writers in the later seasons of The Office.
投诉之塔这条副线是《办公室》后期编剧们非常喜欢的那种群像戏，对他们来说太有用了。

1672
01:12:45.830 --> 01:12:50.610
When we have 14 characters in the show and we have to give them all something to do.
当我们剧中有14个角色，必须给每个人都安排点事情做的时候。

1673
01:12:50.770 --> 01:12:54.310
So this one takes up eight characters and that's really useful to the writers.
所以这条线用掉了八个角色，这对编剧来说真的太有用了。

1674
01:12:54.510 --> 01:12:59.610
What was so fun about this episode was how funny Jenna was in it.
这一集最有趣的地方在于珍娜在里面表现得有多搞笑。

1675
01:12:59.750 --> 01:13:03.530
So often Pam's character is the emotional heart of the story.
通常帕姆这个角色是故事的情感核心。

1676
01:13:03.750 --> 01:13:08.430
And her relationship with Jim is the romantic subplot that is driving so much of the series.
她和吉姆的关系是推动整部剧发展的重要浪漫副线。

1677
01:13:08.590 --> 01:13:11.630
But it is so delightful when Jenna gets to be funny.
但当珍娜有机会变得搞笑时，真的是太令人高兴了。

1678
01:13:11.630 --> 01:13:20.990
And the writers took a lot of pleasure in figuring out how to make this proper character funny by forcing her to fail.
编剧们花了很多心思去琢磨如何通过迫使这个正派角色失败，来让她变得搞笑。

1679
01:13:21.250 --> 01:13:29.630
And you'll notice that in the final prank phone call that she makes to lose a client, the laugh doesn't come on the yo mama joke.
你会注意到，在她为了气走客户而打的最后那个恶作剧电话里，笑点并不是在那个“你妈”的笑话上。

1680
01:13:29.810 --> 01:13:37.590
It comes on Pam having to over explain the yo mama joke because she's never had to deliver an insult like this before.
笑点在于帕姆不得不对那个“你妈”的笑话进行过度解释，因为她以前从来没说过这种侮辱人的话。

1681
01:13:37.590 --> 01:13:45.730
It's a classic example of the laugh coming, not on the cleverness of the joke itself, but on the performance of the actor.
这是一个经典的例子，笑点不在于笑话本身的机智，而在于演员的表演。

1682
01:13:45.950 --> 01:13:46.970
And Jenna just nails it.
而珍娜简直演绝了。

1683
01:13:47.830 --> 01:13:55.690
Lady, my favorite thing about Brent sending in audio clips is that they always include like high praise for you and I.
莱迪，我最喜欢布伦特发来音频剪辑的一点是，里面总包含对你和我的高度赞扬。

1684
01:13:56.630 --> 01:13:57.310
I know, Brent.
我懂的，布伦特。

1685
01:13:57.310 --> 01:13:59.090
And they make me feel so good about myself.
它们让我对自己的感觉好极了。

1686
01:13:59.490 --> 01:14:01.030
Brent, thank you so much.
布伦特，非常感谢。

1687
01:14:01.030 --> 01:14:13.870
But one of the other things I really appreciate about Brent's perspective on episodes is he always takes it back to what moves the story, what makes the joke happen.
但对于布伦特对剧集的看法，我非常欣赏的另一点是，他总是能回归到是什么推动了故事，是什么促成了笑话。

1688
01:14:14.350 --> 01:14:19.390
I can just hear what a great teacher he is because he's so right.
我简直能听出他是一位多么优秀的老师，因为他说得太对了。

1689
01:14:19.830 --> 01:14:22.870
The thing that's funny about it isn't the yo mama joke.
真正好笑的地方根本不是那个“你妈”的笑话。

1690
01:14:23.070 --> 01:14:28.670
It's Pam getting so flustered and trying so earnestly to really be off-putting.
而是帕姆变得那么慌乱，还那么认真地想要去恶心别人。

1691
01:14:28.670 --> 01:14:29.290
Yes.
是的。

1692
01:14:29.690 --> 01:14:31.570
Speaking of, Brent is a teacher.
说到这儿，布伦特确实是个老师。

1693
01:14:31.790 --> 01:14:33.670
He teaches comedy writing classes.
他教喜剧写作课。

1694
01:14:33.990 --> 01:14:34.270
Yes.
没错。

1695
01:14:34.430 --> 01:14:37.490
And you can sign up for his classes at brentforrester.com.
你可以在 brentforrester.com 报名他的课程。

1696
01:14:37.690 --> 01:14:39.130
And you know I'll put it in stories.
你们知道我会把它发到快拍里的。

1697
01:14:39.330 --> 01:14:40.030
Yes, she will.
是的，她会的。

1698
01:14:40.450 --> 01:14:50.930
Well, this storyline ends with everybody back in the annex and they put Pam's complaint on the top of the tower and it's almost brushing the ceiling tiles and everyone cheers.
好吧，这条故事线的结尾是大家回到了分办公室，他们把帕姆的投诉信放在塔顶，都快碰到天花板瓷砖了，然后大家都欢呼起来。

1699
01:14:51.550 --> 01:14:53.530
Yeah, Pam saved the day.
耶，帕姆拯救了世界。

1700
01:14:53.530 --> 01:14:54.310
Yes,
是的，

1701
01:14:54.470 --> 01:15:06.770
but we learn a little more information about how her insult was truly terrible because I guess this woman had recently passed away and had struggled with obesity her whole life.
但我们了解到更多关于她的侮辱为何极其恶劣的信息，因为我猜这位女士最近刚去世，而且她一生都在与肥胖作斗争。

1702
01:15:07.010 --> 01:15:11.490
The client's mother had just recently passed away, which is why it wasn't just a complaint card.
客户的母亲最近刚去世，这就是为什么这不仅仅是一张投诉卡。

1703
01:15:11.630 --> 01:15:13.650
It was, you don't get our business anymore.
而是，你们再也别想做我们的生意了。

1704
01:15:13.750 --> 01:15:14.030
Yes.
是的。

1705
01:15:14.110 --> 01:15:14.530
This is horrible.
这太可怕了。

1706
01:15:14.530 --> 01:15:17.570
And Pam wants you to know I did not know any of that information.
而且帕姆想让你知道，我当时完全不知道这些信息。

1707
01:15:17.570 --> 01:15:18.730
I am so very sorry.
我真的非常抱歉。

1708
01:15:18.730 --> 01:15:19.510
Of course not.
当然没有。

1709
01:15:19.870 --> 01:15:22.490
But everyone's happy.
但大家都很高兴。

1710
01:15:22.790 --> 01:15:23.830
They built a tower.
他们建造了一座塔。

1711
01:15:25.050 --> 01:15:26.430
That's what they did that day.
那是他们那一天做的事情。

1712
01:15:26.910 --> 01:15:27.890
So simple.
如此简单。

1713
01:15:28.090 --> 01:15:28.650
So simple.
如此简单。

1714
01:15:28.770 --> 01:15:29.230
And lovely.
而且很可爱。

1715
01:15:30.290 --> 01:15:39.910
We also got a fan question about this scene from Royelle L in Boise, Idaho, who said, I have been waiting for years to submit this.
我们还收到了爱达荷州博伊西的罗伊尔·L关于这个场景的一个粉丝提问，他说，我等了好几年才来提问。

1716
01:15:40.070 --> 01:15:45.950
It always makes me so happy when we can, like, answer a question for someone that has been, like, years in making.
每当我们可以为某人解答一个酝酿了多年的问题时，我总是感到非常高兴。

1717
01:15:45.950 --> 01:15:46.730
Waiting for the episode.
等待这一集。

1718
01:15:46.930 --> 01:15:47.150
Yes.
是的。

1719
01:15:48.730 --> 01:15:48.790
Great.
太棒了。

1720
01:15:48.850 --> 01:15:49.550
Here's the question.
问题是这样的。

1721
01:15:49.830 --> 01:15:56.030
When Creed is congratulating Pam for her first customer complaint, why is he in gray sweatpants?
当克里德祝贺帕姆接到第一个客户投诉时，他为什么穿着灰色运动裤？

1722
01:15:56.430 --> 01:16:00.610
I also noticed he has his business shirt tucked into his sweatpants.
我还注意到他把商务衬衫扎进了运动裤里。

1723
01:16:00.850 --> 01:16:02.490
This is such a funny detail.
这是一个非常有趣的细节。

1724
01:16:02.850 --> 01:16:08.990
Well, Royelle, I noticed this too, and I was curious, so I went to the shooting draft and I found the answer.
嗯，罗伊尔，我也注意到了这一点，我很好奇，所以我去看了拍摄剧本，找到了答案。

1725
01:16:09.350 --> 01:16:13.670
It was actually explained at the very top of the episode, and here's how the script read.
其实在这一集的开头就解释过了，剧本是这样写的。

1726
01:16:14.190 --> 01:16:16.070
Jim and Pam walk in for the day.
吉姆和帕姆走进办公室开始一天的工作。

1727
01:16:16.070 --> 01:16:20.810
Pam is wearing painting clothes, a paint-flecked sweatshirt and jeans.
帕姆穿着画画的衣服，一件沾满油漆斑点的卫衣和牛仔裤。

1728
01:16:21.150 --> 01:16:23.630
Dwight says, well, it finally happened.
德怀特说，好吧，这一天终于来了。

1729
01:16:23.830 --> 01:16:24.710
Pam, stop caring.
帕姆，你终于不在乎了。

1730
01:16:25.390 --> 01:16:27.210
Creed says, welcome aboard, Pam.
克里德说，欢迎加入，帕姆。

1731
01:16:27.450 --> 01:16:31.930
And in the stage direction, it says, Creed is wearing sweatpants and Crocs.
舞台说明中写道，克里德穿着运动裤和洞洞鞋。

1732
01:16:31.930 --> 01:16:34.450
Oh, wow, that's great.
哦，哇，太棒了。

1733
01:16:34.470 --> 01:16:37.150
And then Pam says, these are my painting clothes.
然后帕姆说，这些是我的画画衣服。

1734
01:16:37.710 --> 01:16:41.390
Isn't it funny how you trim out one line?
只剪掉一句台词不是很搞笑吗？

1735
01:16:41.650 --> 01:16:41.990
Yeah.
是的。

1736
01:16:42.390 --> 01:16:46.190
And now for this whole episode, we have the mystery of why is Creed wearing sweatpants?
而现在在整整这一集里，我们都有这样一个谜团：克里德为什么要穿运动裤？

1737
01:16:46.410 --> 01:16:50.150
I bet Creed was so happy to be wearing sweatpants and Crocs all week.
我敢打赌，克里德这一周能穿着运动裤和洞洞鞋一定高兴坏了。

1738
01:16:50.150 --> 01:16:53.750
Like, he was probably like, we should make this a weekly thing.
就像，他可能在想，我们应该把这变成每周的惯例。

1739
01:16:54.410 --> 01:17:01.610
Back in the alleyway, the guys have stopped tussling, and Angela now has suddenly appeared behind Oscar.
回到小巷里，大伙们已经停止了拉扯，安吉拉现在突然出现在奥斯卡身后。

1740
01:17:01.910 --> 01:17:02.190
Yeah.
是的。

1741
01:17:02.610 --> 01:17:03.750
And he's going to yell at her.
然后他要对她大喊大叫了。

1742
01:17:03.870 --> 01:17:08.930
He's going to be like, I cannot believe you hired someone to beat me with a pipe.
他会说，我真不敢相信你雇人拿水管打我。

1743
01:17:08.930 --> 01:17:13.550
And he says, look, what I did was wrong, and I have to live with that every day, but your husband is gay.
他说，听着，我做的事是错的，我每天都要为此承担后果，但你丈夫是个同性恋。

1744
01:17:13.730 --> 01:17:15.490
And he was gay when you married him.
而且当你嫁给他的时候他就是。

1745
01:17:15.550 --> 01:17:16.550
And Angela's like, no.
安吉拉却说，不。

1746
01:17:17.250 --> 01:17:22.730
And Oscar says, Angela, until you face that, you're going to be confused and angry for all the wrong reasons.
奥斯卡说，安吉拉，直到你正视这一点，你都会因为各种错误的理由而感到困惑和愤怒。

1747
01:17:22.890 --> 01:17:25.390
But if you want to blame me for the whole thing, go ahead.
但如果你想把整件事都怪在我头上，那就来吧。

1748
01:17:25.510 --> 01:17:26.410
I won't stop you.
我不会阻止你的。

1749
01:17:26.790 --> 01:17:27.190
Hit me.
打我吧。

1750
01:17:27.350 --> 01:17:28.430
You have my blessing.
我批准了。

1751
01:17:28.750 --> 01:17:29.250
Hit me.
来吧。

1752
01:17:30.390 --> 01:17:31.570
And Angela's like, okay.
然后安吉拉就说，好吧。

1753
01:17:31.710 --> 01:17:32.750
And she grabs the pipe.
接着她抓起了管子。

1754
01:17:32.810 --> 01:17:34.470
I know, but he won't let go of it.
我知道，但他就是不肯松手。

1755
01:17:34.990 --> 01:17:37.330
And she says, are you going to let go of it?
然后她说，你到底放不放手？

1756
01:17:37.330 --> 01:17:39.430
Because part of the blame is definitely on you.
因为你绝对也有责任。

1757
01:17:39.630 --> 01:17:42.810
And then Oscar says, Angela, it's a lead freaking pipe.
接着奥斯卡说，安吉拉，那可是根该死的铅管。

1758
01:17:42.990 --> 01:17:44.510
And then Angela just kicks him.
然后安吉拉直接踢了他。

1759
01:17:44.730 --> 01:17:46.110
How did that work, Angela?
那是怎么做到的，安吉拉？

1760
01:17:46.350 --> 01:17:48.210
Did you just fake kick him?
你是假踢他的吗？

1761
01:17:48.290 --> 01:17:49.030
Did he have a pad?
他戴护具了吗？

1762
01:17:49.330 --> 01:17:51.530
I kicked him, and he had a pad on his shin.
我踢了他，他胫骨上确实戴着护具。

1763
01:17:51.650 --> 01:17:52.570
Like a shin guard.
就像护腿板一样。

1764
01:17:52.670 --> 01:17:54.590
He had a shin guard, but I really kicked him.
他戴了护腿板，但我确实狠狠地踢了他。

1765
01:17:54.750 --> 01:17:56.470
Okay, because it looked like a real kick.
好吧，因为看起来像真踢一样。

1766
01:17:56.590 --> 01:17:57.090
It was.
本来就是。

1767
01:17:57.230 --> 01:17:57.490
Okay.
好吧。

1768
01:17:58.270 --> 01:18:03.190
And then Angela very emotionally says, you were supposed to be my friend.
然后安吉拉情绪激动地说，你本来该是我的朋友的。

1769
01:18:03.550 --> 01:18:03.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1770
01:18:04.450 --> 01:18:07.170
And then later, Angela is crying.
后来，安吉拉哭了。

1771
01:18:07.330 --> 01:18:09.970
On a bench outside, and Dwight joins her.
坐在外面的长椅上，德怀特走过去陪她。

1772
01:18:10.270 --> 01:18:12.830
And she says, I just feel so stupid.
她说，我觉得自己太蠢了。

1773
01:18:13.510 --> 01:18:15.710
I sit next to him every day.
我每天都坐在他旁边。

1774
01:18:16.950 --> 01:18:21.110
So lady, this is a line that's quoted to me a lot.
所以女士们先生们，这句台词经常有人对我引用。

1775
01:18:21.350 --> 01:18:21.810
Okay.
好吧。

1776
01:18:21.970 --> 01:18:22.890
This is one of those lines.
这就是那种台词之一。

1777
01:18:23.270 --> 01:18:24.630
And Rain gets it too.
雷恩也经常听到这句话。

1778
01:18:24.750 --> 01:18:25.570
You're not stupid.
你一点也不蠢。

1779
01:18:25.730 --> 01:18:26.550
Jazz is stupid.
爵士乐才蠢。

1780
01:18:26.830 --> 01:18:28.890
And then I say, jazz is stupid.
然后我说，爵士乐真蠢。

1781
01:18:29.030 --> 01:18:30.530
I mean, just play the right notes.
我是说，弹对音符不就好了。

1782
01:18:30.530 --> 01:18:32.230
It's such a funny thing to say.
这话真是太搞笑了。

1783
01:18:32.490 --> 01:18:34.090
And then Dwight says, I know.
然后德怀特说，我知道。

1784
01:18:34.270 --> 01:18:35.570
You're going to be okay, monkey.
你会没事的，小猴子。

1785
01:18:35.570 --> 01:18:39.630
And then the last couplet of dialogue was completely improvised.
然后最后两句对话完全是即兴发挥的。

1786
01:18:39.950 --> 01:18:40.890
About Trevor?
关于特雷弗？

1787
01:18:41.450 --> 01:18:44.110
I say, I don't like your friend Trevor.
我说，我讨厌你的朋友特雷弗。

1788
01:18:44.430 --> 01:18:46.790
And then Rain says, I don't like him either.
然后雷恩说，我也不喜欢他。

1789
01:18:47.030 --> 01:18:48.690
And yet I really like him.
然而我其实挺喜欢他的。

1790
01:18:49.150 --> 01:18:50.410
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

1791
01:18:50.410 --> 01:18:52.050
I can't believe that was improvised.
真不敢相信那是即兴发挥的。

1792
01:18:52.490 --> 01:18:53.370
And it made it in.
而且还被剪进正片了。

1793
01:18:53.370 --> 01:18:56.410
And I was so tickled when I saw it.
我看到的时候高兴坏了。

1794
01:18:57.170 --> 01:19:02.150
Because, you know, with me crying and Dwight puts his arm around me, they left the camera there for a bit.
因为你知道的，当时我在哭，德怀特搂着我，摄影机在那里多停了一会儿。

1795
01:19:02.250 --> 01:19:02.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1796
01:19:02.670 --> 01:19:05.010
And so I just said, I don't like your friend Trevor.
所以我当时就脱口而出，我讨厌你的朋友特雷弗。

1797
01:19:05.390 --> 01:19:06.870
Such a funny thing to say.
这话太逗了。

1798
01:19:07.150 --> 01:19:09.710
And then Dwight has such a great response.
然后德怀特的反应绝了。

1799
01:19:09.810 --> 01:19:11.250
And then Rain's response is perfection.
接着雷恩的回答堪称完美。

1800
01:19:11.250 --> 01:19:14.090
We got a fan question from Jennifer C.
我们收到了一个来自珍妮弗·C的粉丝提问。

1801
01:19:14.210 --> 01:19:16.410
in Colorado Springs, Colorado, who said,
在科罗拉多州科罗拉多斯普林斯，有人说，

1802
01:19:16.610 --> 01:19:19.430
This is something I've wondered for years.
这是我多年来一直想知道的事。

1803
01:19:19.990 --> 01:19:22.510
Does Mike sure hate jazz?
迈克是不是真的很讨厌爵士乐？

1804
01:19:23.110 --> 01:19:23.590
Oh.
哦。

1805
01:19:23.870 --> 01:19:28.630
I know he didn't write this episode, but this theme pops up in a lot of his projects.
我知道这集不是他写的，但这个主题在他的很多作品里都出现过。

1806
01:19:28.630 --> 01:19:31.330
And then Jennifer cites all these projects.
然后珍妮弗列举了所有这些作品。

1807
01:19:31.590 --> 01:19:35.650
The Good Place, Season 1, Episode 9, someone says,
《善地》第一季第九集，有人说，

1808
01:19:35.810 --> 01:19:37.090
Ugh, I hate jazz.
呃，我讨厌爵士乐。

1809
01:19:37.310 --> 01:19:38.470
It's like, we get it.
这就好比，我们懂了。

1810
01:19:38.650 --> 01:19:39.810
Wrap it up, Elton John.
行了行了，埃尔顿·约翰。

1811
01:19:40.750 --> 01:19:46.410
In Parks and Recreation, in Season 5, Episode 12, someone says,
在《公园与游憩》第五季第12集里，有人说，

1812
01:19:46.870 --> 01:19:48.610
You'd really want to get to know the guy, right?
你真的很想了解这个人，对吧？

1813
01:19:48.770 --> 01:19:53.790
You'd want to know his personality, his favorite season of Friends, whether he hates jazz.
你会想了解他的性格，他最喜欢的《老友记》季度，以及他是否讨厌爵士乐。

1814
01:19:53.990 --> 01:19:55.070
Hopefully he does.
希望他是讨厌的。

1815
01:19:55.670 --> 01:19:57.270
There is a theme here.
这里面有个主题。

1816
01:19:57.270 --> 01:19:59.730
Yes, and then jazz is stupid.
是的，然后就是爵士乐太蠢了。

1817
01:20:00.090 --> 01:20:01.370
Just play the right notes.
只要弹对音符就行了。

1818
01:20:01.950 --> 01:20:05.750
Jennifer said, These are just three examples, but there are so many more.
珍妮弗说，这只是三个例子，但还有更多。

1819
01:20:06.210 --> 01:20:07.350
Please explain.
请解释一下。

1820
01:20:08.230 --> 01:20:12.670
So, one of my favorite things with our podcast is to reach out to people.
所以，在我们的播客中，我最喜欢的事情之一就是联系大家。

1821
01:20:12.930 --> 01:20:13.890
Please tell me.
快告诉我吧。

1822
01:20:13.890 --> 01:20:16.090
You texted Mike Schur about this.
你为此给迈克·舒尔发了短信。

1823
01:20:16.230 --> 01:20:16.450
I did.
我发了。

1824
01:20:16.670 --> 01:20:17.450
What did he say?
他说什么了？

1825
01:20:17.650 --> 01:20:20.250
He wrote back, Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.
他回信说，哈哈哈哈哈哈哈。

1826
01:20:21.790 --> 01:20:24.650
You can tell, Jennifer, I don't hate jazz.
你可以看出来，珍妮弗，我不讨厌爵士乐。

1827
01:20:24.930 --> 01:20:27.130
I didn't even write all of those jokes.
那些笑话甚至都不是我一个人写的。

1828
01:20:27.270 --> 01:20:40.450
But comedy writers like to pick on jazz because, like most art forms, it has a certain group of adherents who like to lecture you on why it's so amazing and so cool and so special.
但喜剧编剧喜欢拿爵士乐开涮，因为就像大多数艺术形式一样，它有一群坚定的拥趸，喜欢向你长篇大论它为什么那么棒、那么酷、那么特别。

1829
01:20:40.870 --> 01:20:46.570
Mike said, kind of like the Ryan Gosling character in La La Land where he explains jazz to John Legend.
迈克说，有点像《爱乐之城》里瑞恩·高斯林的角色向约翰·传奇解释爵士乐那样。

1830
01:20:47.910 --> 01:20:56.730
Mike said, comedy writers in general have a disdain for anything that causes people to wax poetic or why you just don't get something.
迈克说，喜剧编剧普遍对任何让人夸夸其谈或觉得“你不懂”的事物有一种蔑视。

1831
01:20:56.970 --> 01:20:59.590
And he said, jazz is one of those things.
他说，爵士乐就是其中之一。

1832
01:20:59.590 --> 01:21:01.710
What a perfect answer.
多么完美的回答。

1833
01:21:01.950 --> 01:21:02.270
I know.
我知道。

1834
01:21:02.590 --> 01:21:03.710
I love that.
我太喜欢这个回答了。

1835
01:21:03.910 --> 01:21:09.630
Well, I love that Jennifer keyed in on this joke about jazz that keeps popping up.
嗯，我很喜欢珍妮弗注意到了这个不断出现的关于爵士乐的笑话。

1836
01:21:10.170 --> 01:21:19.830
